{"entries":{"tdata:src/doclet.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"VOID_RETURN","longname":"VOID_RETURN","name":"VOID_RETURN","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Matches `void` and `void | undefined` return types (no `@returns` needed).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":71},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:71","src":"src/doclet.ts:112"},"level":0},{"id":"injectCheckerTypes","longname":"injectCheckerTypes","name":"injectCheckerTypes","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Fills in/upgrades parameter and return types from the TypeScript checker.\nOnly applied to `.ts`-family sources; JS files keep their JSDoc annotations.\n\nSemantics:\n- Every documented parameter gets its `type.names` replaced by the checker\n  type (TS is the source of truth for `.ts` files) when a same-named\n  parameter exists in the signature.\n- The return type is always upgraded to the checker's return type; if the\n  doclet has no `@returns` but the function returns a non-`void` type, a\n  returns entry is added.","params":[{"description":"The doclets to enrich (mutated in place).","name":"doclets","type":{"names":["readonly DmdDoclet[]"]}},{"description":"The project's shared type program.","name":"program","type":{"names":["TypeProgram"]}},{"description":"Absolute path of the source file the doclets came from.","name":"srcAbsPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":32},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:32","src":"src/doclet.ts:72"},"level":0},{"id":"injectCheckerType","longname":"injectCheckerType","name":"injectCheckerType","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Applies the checker types to one doclet, when both sides exist.","params":[{"description":"The doclet to enrich (mutated in place).","name":"doclet","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet"]}},{"description":"The project's shared type program.","name":"program","type":{"names":["TypeProgram"]}},{"description":"Absolute path of the source file the doclet came from.","name":"srcAbsPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":44},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:44","src":"src/doclet.ts:87"},"level":0},{"id":"upgradeParamTypes","longname":"upgradeParamTypes","name":"upgradeParamTypes","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Replaces each same-named parameter's JSDoc type with the checker's type.","params":[{"description":"The doclet whose `params` are upgraded (mutated in place).","name":"doclet","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet"]}},{"description":"The extracted signature for the doclet's symbol.","name":"info","type":{"names":["SymbolType"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":59},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:59","src":"src/doclet.ts:101"},"level":0},{"id":"injectPointers","longname":"injectPointers","name":"injectPointers","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Attaches the `src`/`dist` pointer to every doclet. `pointers` maps a\ndoclet's identity (its `meta.lineno` in the generated file) — see the\nresolve/render pipeline for how it is built.","params":[{"description":"The doclets to annotate (mutated in place).","name":"doclets","type":{"names":["readonly DmdDoclet[]"]}},{"description":"`meta.lineno` → pointer, produced by the render pipeline.","name":"pointers","type":{"names":["ReadonlyMap<number, SymbolPointer>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":79},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:79","src":"src/doclet.ts:121"},"level":0},{"id":"normalizeDoclets","longname":"normalizeDoclets","name":"normalizeDoclets","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Normalizes dmd input doclets in place.\n\n1. For ES-module sources without a `@module` tag (the common case), jsdoc\n   emits top-level class doclets whose `memberof` points at themselves\n   (`id === memberof`). dmd's `#orphans` selector requires `memberof` to be\n   absent, so those symbols never render. Undoing the self-parenting makes\n   them render as top-level symbols; class children keep their (non-self)\n   `memberof` so nesting still works. (A constructor's `memberof` equals\n   the class longname but NOT its own `id` — `Point()` ≠ `Point` — so\n   constructors are unaffected.)\n2. Strips the ESM `exports.` prefix jsdoc 4 leaves on doclet names\n   (`exports.Point` → `Point`) by preferring `longname` when present.","params":[{"description":"The doclets to normalize (mutated in place).","name":"data","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The same array, normalized.","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":106},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:106","src":"src/doclet.ts:147"},"level":0},{"id":"extractLookupKeys","longname":"extractLookupKeys","name":"extractLookupKeys","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Extracts the qualified (`Class.member`) and plain lookup keys for a doclet.","params":[{"description":"The doclet to name.","name":"doclet","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The qualified-first lookup keys, or `null` when the doclet is not nameable.","type":{"names":["SymbolLookup"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":122},"order":6,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:122","src":"src/doclet.ts:164"},"level":0},{"id":"memberofBase","longname":"memberofBase","name":"memberofBase","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Extracts the class base from a jsdoc `memberof` value (`module:f.Point` → `Point`).","params":[{"description":"The raw `memberof` value.","name":"memberof","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The class base, or `null` when empty.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":143},"order":7,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:143","src":"src/doclet.ts:185"},"level":0},{"id":"upgradeReturnType","longname":"upgradeReturnType","name":"upgradeReturnType","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Upgrades (or adds) the doclet's `@returns` entry from the checker type.","params":[{"description":"The doclet whose `returns` are upgraded (mutated in place).","name":"doclet","type":{"names":["DmdDoclet"]}},{"description":"The extracted signature for the doclet's symbol.","name":"info","type":{"names":["SymbolType"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":155},"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/doclet.js:155","src":"src/doclet.ts:197"},"level":0}],"fp":"cd6e4918b6e12025f6e38eed8d640fc3dd111ec767476856fe6061c76ad68abd","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318073,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/index.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"c1bc1c03e4fa372eae8d1bdb1b795a0306100946b20017c2470d515ece3669b4","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318076,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/cli.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"execute","longname":"execute","name":"execute","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Runs the pipeline and prints the summary. Returns the exit code.","params":[{"description":"Positional `rootSrcDir` arguments from the CLI.","name":"roots","type":{"names":["string[]"]}},{"description":"Parsed CLI flags.","name":"options","type":{"names":["CliOptions"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The process exit code (`0` ok / dry-run, `1` on failure).","type":{"names":["Promise<number>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":49},"async":true,"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cli.js:49","src":"src/cli.ts:71"},"level":0},{"id":"formatUnexpected","longname":"formatUnexpected","name":"formatUnexpected","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Formats an unexpected error, honoring MDOCS_DEBUG for stack traces.","params":[{"description":"The unexpected error to format.","name":"error","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The message (plus stack trace when `MDOCS_DEBUG` is set).","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":93},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cli.js:93","src":"src/cli.ts:110"},"level":0},{"id":"parseParallelism","longname":"parseParallelism","name":"parseParallelism","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Parses `--parallelism` into true | false | integer. Range checks live in the config schema.","params":[{"description":"The raw flag value.","name":"value","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true`, `false`, or the parsed integer.","type":{"names":["number | boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":105},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cli.js:105","src":"src/cli.ts:121"},"level":0},{"id":"printSummary","longname":"printSummary","name":"printSummary","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Prints the one-line summary and the failures, if any.","params":[{"description":"The run result to summarize.","name":"result","type":{"names":["RunResult"]}},{"description":"When set, already printed in `printVerbose`; controls the dry-run listing.","name":"verbose","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":121},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cli.js:121","src":"src/cli.ts:136"},"level":0},{"id":"printVerbose","longname":"printVerbose","name":"printVerbose","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Prints resolved settings and per-file details (--verbose).","params":[{"description":"The run result to print.","name":"result","type":{"names":["RunResult"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":150},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cli.js:150","src":"src/cli.ts:162"},"level":0}],"fp":"ed089bc0c50f1ecf3c862ff21f5d9254e16b4d5d029425a9beccd0ce88e27207","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318079,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/config.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"defineConfig","longname":"defineConfig","name":"defineConfig","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Identity helper for typed configs, mirroring vite's `defineConfig`:\n`export default defineConfig({ … })`. Purely an authoring aid — validation\nhappens in `resolveConfig`, after the config is loaded.","params":[{"description":"The typed config object, function, or promise of either.","name":"config","type":{"names":["MdocsConfigExport"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The config export, unchanged.","type":{"names":["MdocsConfigExport"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":38},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:38","src":"src/config.ts:80"},"level":0},{"id":"loadConfig","longname":"loadConfig","name":"loadConfig","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Locates, loads, evaluates and validates the config file for `cwd`.\n\nWhen no config file exists and no explicit path was given, the run falls\nback to the default configuration (vite behavior) and `filePath` is\n`undefined`. An explicit `--config` path that does not exist always\nthrows.\n\n`overrides` (config keys provided out-of-band, e.g. CLI flags or a\nprogrammatic call) are merged over the file's config — an override always\nwins for its own key, everything else comes from the file.","params":[{"description":"Working directory for config lookup and relative roots.","name":"cwd","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Explicit `--config` path (beats auto-discovery).","name":"explicitPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Config keys merged over the file's config.","name":"overrides","type":{"names":["{ cache?: boolean; cachePath?: string; outDirName?: string; parallelism?: number | boolean; rootDistDir?: string; rootSrcDir?: string | string[]; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The resolved config and the file (if any) it came from.","type":{"names":["Promise<{ config: ResolvedMdocsConfig; filePath: string | undefined; }>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":58},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:58","src":"src/config.ts:102"},"level":0},{"id":"resolveConfig","longname":"resolveConfig","name":"resolveConfig","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Resolves and validates a user-facing config into a `ResolvedMdocsConfig`.","params":[{"description":"The user-facing (unvalidated) config.","name":"raw","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The frozen, fully-resolved config.","type":{"names":["ResolvedMdocsConfig"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":85},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:85","src":"src/config.ts:131"},"level":0},{"id":"configLoadError","longname":"configLoadError","name":"configLoadError","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Wraps config-loading failures with a consistent code and message.","params":[{"description":"The config file that failed to load.","name":"filePath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The underlying error.","name":"cause","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A `MdocsError` with code `CONFIG_LOAD_FAILED`.","type":{"names":["MdocsError"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":103},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:103","src":"src/config.ts:150"},"level":0},{"id":"definedOverrides","longname":"definedOverrides","name":"definedOverrides","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Keeps only the keys of `overrides` that are actually set.","params":[{"description":"The user-facing config overrides (any keys missing are kept unset).","name":"overrides","type":{"names":["{ cache?: boolean; cachePath?: string; outDirName?: string; parallelism?: number | boolean; rootDistDir?: string; rootSrcDir?: string | string[]; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The overrides with only the set keys.","type":{"names":["Record<string, unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":112},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:112","src":"src/config.ts:160"},"level":0},{"id":"describeType","longname":"describeType","name":"describeType","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Human-readable description of a value's runtime type.","params":[{"description":"The value to describe.","name":"value","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`null`, `an array`, or the `typeof` string.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":126},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:126","src":"src/config.ts:174"},"level":0},{"id":"evaluateConfigExport","longname":"evaluateConfigExport","name":"evaluateConfigExport","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Resolves the exported value, calling the function form if present.\nPromise exports are resolved transparently: `await` assimilates thenables,\nso by the time the value gets here any promise layers have already settled.","params":[{"description":"The raw module export to resolve.","name":"exported","type":{"names":["unknown"]}},{"description":"The config file it came from (for errors).","name":"filePath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The resolved plain-object config.","type":{"names":["Promise<unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":144},"async":true,"order":6,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:144","src":"src/config.ts:192"},"level":0},{"id":"importConfigModule","longname":"importConfigModule","name":"importConfigModule","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Imports a config module, choosing the loader the same way vite and Node do:\n\n| file        | loader                                                    |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.mjs`      | ESM always                                                |\n| `.cjs`      | `require` (never silently reinterpreted)                  |\n| `.js` + `\"type\": \"module\"`                       | ESM always        |\n| `.js` + `\"type\": \"commonjs\"` or no `package.json` | `require` first,  |\n|             | falling back to a sibling `.mjs` copy only for ESM-in-CJS |\n\n`require()` of an ESM `.js` file fails with a plain `SyntaxError` on current\nNode versions, so `.js` ESM configs in `\"type\": \"commonjs\"` packages load\nthrough the fallback, not through `require(esm)`.","params":[{"description":"The config file to import.","name":"filePath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The module export (namespace object for ESM, as-is for CJS).","type":{"names":["Promise<unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":180},"async":true,"order":7,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:180","src":"src/config.ts:232"},"level":0},{"id":"importEsmInCommonJsPackage","longname":"importEsmInCommonJsPackage","name":"importEsmInCommonJsPackage","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Imports ESM config living in a `.js` file of a CommonJS-typed package.\nThe copy is written **next to the config file** — so relative imports in\nthe config keep working — with a hidden, unique name, removed afterwards.","params":[{"description":"The `.js` config file whose ESM-in-CJS content is loaded.","name":"filePath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The module export.","type":{"names":["Promise<unknown>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":217},"async":true,"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:217","src":"src/config.ts:266"},"level":0},{"id":"isEsmInCjsError","longname":"isEsmInCjsError","name":"isEsmInCjsError","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"True when `error` reports ESM syntax loaded as CommonJS (Node-version-dependent).","params":[{"description":"The catch value to classify.","name":"error","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Whether the error is an ESM-in-CJS load failure.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":238},"order":9,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:238","src":"src/config.ts:290"},"level":0},{"id":"isModuleNamespace","longname":"isModuleNamespace","name":"isModuleNamespace","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Detects a native ESM module namespace exotic object.","params":[{"description":"The value to test.","name":"value","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` for a native ESM module namespace object.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":252},"order":10,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:252","src":"src/config.ts:305"},"level":0},{"id":"locateConfigFile","longname":"locateConfigFile","name":"locateConfigFile","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Finds the config file to use, honoring an explicit `--config` override.","params":[{"description":"Working directory to look up config files in.","name":"cwd","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Explicit `--config` path (never auto-discovered).","name":"explicitPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute path, or `undefined` when none exists and none was given.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":261},"async":true,"order":11,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:261","src":"src/config.ts:315"},"level":0},{"id":"nearestPackageType","longname":"nearestPackageType","name":"nearestPackageType","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Nearest `package.json` `\"type\"` walking up from `filePath` (or undefined).","params":[{"description":"The config file to start from.","name":"filePath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`module`, `commonjs`, or `undefined` when no nearest `package.json` declares it.","type":{"names":["\"commonjs\" | \"module\""]}}],"meta":{"lineno":290},"order":12,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:290","src":"src/config.ts:344"},"level":0},{"id":"resolveParallelism","longname":"resolveParallelism","name":"resolveParallelism","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Resolves the effective worker count (\"true\" = all cores).","params":[{"description":"The user-facing `parallelism` (boolean or number).","name":"value","type":{"names":["number | boolean"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The concrete worker count.","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":314},"order":13,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/config.js:314","src":"src/config.ts:366"},"level":0}],"fp":"fb26f95660d5672aa2d5bf52f28fb96a26f53182becdfe2f5d7c0790f227d39d","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318085,"symbols":0},"md:src/index.ts":{"fp":"4119e302411e8e2a1cc60fe2caac16eb5be08a1b9d0d1f6be4a50f0cf9e6bce7","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0},"md:src/doclet.ts":{"fp":"0f5c7b25392c5b98ed621228553d1bf391b48578bb6f230a2be8c54a7e2f2c23","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#VOID_RETURN\">VOID_RETURN</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Matches <code>void</code> and <code>void | undefined</code> return types (no <code>@returns</code> needed).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#injectCheckerTypes\">injectCheckerTypes(doclets, program, srcAbsPath)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Fills in/upgrades parameter and return types from the TypeScript checker.\nOnly applied to <code>.ts</code>-family sources; JS files keep their JSDoc annotations.</p>\n<p>Semantics:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every documented parameter gets its <code>type.names</code> replaced by the checker\ntype (TS is the source of truth for <code>.ts</code> files) when a same-named\nparameter exists in the signature.</li>\n<li>The return type is always upgraded to the checker&#39;s return type; if the\ndoclet has no <code>@returns</code> but the function returns a non-<code>void</code> type, a\nreturns entry is added.</li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#injectCheckerType\">injectCheckerType(doclet, program, srcAbsPath)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Applies the checker types to one doclet, when both sides exist.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#upgradeParamTypes\">upgradeParamTypes(doclet, info)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Replaces each same-named parameter&#39;s JSDoc type with the checker&#39;s type.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#injectPointers\">injectPointers(doclets, pointers)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Attaches the <code>src</code>/<code>dist</code> pointer to every doclet. <code>pointers</code> maps a\ndoclet&#39;s identity (its <code>meta.lineno</code> in the generated file) — see the\nresolve/render pipeline for how it is built.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#normalizeDoclets\">normalizeDoclets(data)</a> ⇒ <code>DmdDoclet[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalizes dmd input doclets in place.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>For ES-module sources without a <code>@module</code> tag (the common case), jsdoc\nemits top-level class doclets whose <code>memberof</code> points at themselves\n(<code>id === memberof</code>). dmd&#39;s <code>#orphans</code> selector requires <code>memberof</code> to be\nabsent, so those symbols never render. Undoing the self-parenting makes\nthem render as top-level symbols; class children keep their (non-self)\n<code>memberof</code> so nesting still works. (A constructor&#39;s <code>memberof</code> equals\nthe class longname but NOT its own <code>id</code> — <code>Point()</code> ≠ <code>Point</code> — so\nconstructors are unaffected.)</li>\n<li>Strips the ESM <code>exports.</code> prefix jsdoc 4 leaves on doclet names\n(<code>exports.Point</code> → <code>Point</code>) by preferring <code>longname</code> when present.</li>\n</ol>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#extractLookupKeys\">extractLookupKeys(doclet)</a> ⇒ <code>SymbolLookup</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Extracts the qualified (<code>Class.member</code>) and plain lookup keys for a doclet.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#memberofBase\">memberofBase(memberof)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Extracts the class base from a jsdoc <code>memberof</code> value (<code>module:f.Point</code> → <code>Point</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#upgradeReturnType\">upgradeReturnType(doclet, info)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Upgrades (or adds) the doclet&#39;s <code>@returns</code> entry from the checker type.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"VOID_RETURN\"></a>\n\n## VOID\\_RETURN\nMatches `void` and `void | undefined` return types (no `@returns` needed).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/doclet.ts:112  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:71\n<a name=\"injectCheckerTypes\"></a>\n\n## injectCheckerTypes(doclets, program, srcAbsPath)\nFills in/upgrades parameter and return types from the TypeScript checker.\nOnly applied to `.ts`-family sources; JS files keep their JSDoc annotations.\n\nSemantics:\n- Every documented parameter gets its `type.names` replaced by the checker\n  type (TS is the source of truth for `.ts` files) when a same-named\n  parameter exists in the signature.\n- The return type is always upgraded to the checker's return type; if the\n  doclet has no `@returns` but the function returns a non-`void` type, a\n  returns entry is added.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclets | <code>readonly DmdDoclet[]</code> | The doclets to enrich (mutated in place). |\n| program | <code>TypeProgram</code> | The project's shared type program. |\n| srcAbsPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the source file the doclets came from. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:72  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:32\n<a name=\"injectCheckerType\"></a>\n\n## injectCheckerType(doclet, program, srcAbsPath)\nApplies the checker types to one doclet, when both sides exist.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclet | <code>DmdDoclet</code> | The doclet to enrich (mutated in place). |\n| program | <code>TypeProgram</code> | The project's shared type program. |\n| srcAbsPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the source file the doclet came from. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:87  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:44\n<a name=\"upgradeParamTypes\"></a>\n\n## upgradeParamTypes(doclet, info)\nReplaces each same-named parameter's JSDoc type with the checker's type.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclet | <code>DmdDoclet</code> | The doclet whose `params` are upgraded (mutated in place). |\n| info | <code>SymbolType</code> | The extracted signature for the doclet's symbol. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:101  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:59\n<a name=\"injectPointers\"></a>\n\n## injectPointers(doclets, pointers)\nAttaches the `src`/`dist` pointer to every doclet. `pointers` maps a\ndoclet's identity (its `meta.lineno` in the generated file) — see the\nresolve/render pipeline for how it is built.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclets | <code>readonly DmdDoclet[]</code> | The doclets to annotate (mutated in place). |\n| pointers | <code>ReadonlyMap&lt;number, SymbolPointer&gt;</code> | `meta.lineno` → pointer, produced by the render pipeline. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:121  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:79\n<a name=\"normalizeDoclets\"></a>\n\n## normalizeDoclets(data) ⇒ <code>DmdDoclet[]</code>\nNormalizes dmd input doclets in place.\n\n1. For ES-module sources without a `@module` tag (the common case), jsdoc\n   emits top-level class doclets whose `memberof` points at themselves\n   (`id === memberof`). dmd's `#orphans` selector requires `memberof` to be\n   absent, so those symbols never render. Undoing the self-parenting makes\n   them render as top-level symbols; class children keep their (non-self)\n   `memberof` so nesting still works. (A constructor's `memberof` equals\n   the class longname but NOT its own `id` — `Point()` ≠ `Point` — so\n   constructors are unaffected.)\n2. Strips the ESM `exports.` prefix jsdoc 4 leaves on doclet names\n   (`exports.Point` → `Point`) by preferring `longname` when present.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>DmdDoclet[]</code> - The same array, normalized.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| data | <code>DmdDoclet[]</code> | The doclets to normalize (mutated in place). |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:147  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:106\n<a name=\"extractLookupKeys\"></a>\n\n## extractLookupKeys(doclet) ⇒ <code>SymbolLookup</code>\nExtracts the qualified (`Class.member`) and plain lookup keys for a doclet.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>SymbolLookup</code> - The qualified-first lookup keys, or `null` when the doclet is not nameable.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclet | <code>DmdDoclet</code> | The doclet to name. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:164  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:122\n<a name=\"memberofBase\"></a>\n\n## memberofBase(memberof) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nExtracts the class base from a jsdoc `memberof` value (`module:f.Point` → `Point`).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The class base, or `null` when empty.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| memberof | <code>string</code> | The raw `memberof` value. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:185  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:143\n<a name=\"upgradeReturnType\"></a>\n\n## upgradeReturnType(doclet, info)\nUpgrades (or adds) the doclet's `@returns` entry from the checker type.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| doclet | <code>DmdDoclet</code> | The doclet whose `returns` are upgraded (mutated in place). |\n| info | <code>SymbolType</code> | The extracted signature for the doclet's symbol. |\n\nsrc: src/doclet.ts:197  \ndist: dist/doclet.js:155\n","symbols":9},"tdata:src/cache.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES","longname":"MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES","name":"MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Keep in sync with the zod caps in `schema.js`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":45},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:45","src":"src/cache.ts:49"},"level":0},{"id":"MAX_DOCLETS","longname":"MAX_DOCLETS","name":"MAX_DOCLETS","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Keep in sync with the zod cap in `schema.js`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":47},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:47","src":"src/cache.ts:51"},"level":0},{"id":"CACHE_FORMAT","longname":"CACHE_FORMAT","name":"CACHE_FORMAT","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Cache format version — bump on incompatible entry changes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":49},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:49","src":"src/cache.ts:54"},"level":0},{"id":"CACHE_CAP","longname":"CACHE_CAP","name":"CACHE_CAP","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Maximum entries kept; least-recently-used are evicted first.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":51},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:51","src":"src/cache.ts:56"},"level":0},{"id":"RENDER_FORMAT","longname":"RENDER_FORMAT","name":"RENDER_FORMAT","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Distinguishes cache behavior across renderer/output-format changes.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":53},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:53","src":"src/cache.ts:58"},"level":0},{"id":"DTS_SWEEP_CAP","longname":"DTS_SWEEP_CAP","name":"DTS_SWEEP_CAP","kin