ce file.","name":"args.file.absPath"},{"description":"The source extension (e.g. `.ts`).","name":"args.file.extension"},{"description":"The source text (already read by the caller).","name":"args.srcText"},{"description":"Dist-side material from {@link distMaterialOf}, or `null`.","name":"args.distMaterial"},{"description":"Whether the file is `.ts`-family.","name":"args.isTypeScript"},{"description":"{@link programFingerprint} of the run, or `null` for .js.","name":"args.programFp"},{"description":"{@link toolchainFingerprint} of the run.","name":"args.toolchainFp"}],"returns":[{"description":"The fingerprints and both tier keys.","type":{"names":["FileFingerprints"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":153},"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:153","src":"src/cache.ts:188"},"level":0},{"id":"lockfileFingerprint","longname":"lockfileFingerprint","name":"lockfileFingerprint","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"The sha256 of the lockfile in `cwd`, or `undefined` when absent/unreadable.","params":[{"description":"The run's working directory.","name":"cwd","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The lockfile digest.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":176},"order":9,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:176","src":"src/cache.ts:220"},"level":0},{"id":"programFingerprint","longname":"programFingerprint","name":"programFingerprint","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"The whole-program fingerprint for .ts files — every source and declaration\nfile under the project roots, plus the lockfile and the TypeScript version.\nCovers first-party `.d.ts` files that are imported but never roots.\nNode_modules trees behind a lockfile are pinned by the lockfile hash; trees\ndrifted from their lockfile (postinstall patches) can serve stale types.","params":[{"description":"The inputs to fingerprint.","name":"args"},{"description":"Absolute paths of every `.ts`-family file in the run (in any order).","name":"args.tsFiles"},{"description":"Absolute paths of every `.d.ts` under the project roots (in any order).","name":"args.sweep"},{"description":"sha256 of the lockfile, or `undefined` when absent.","name":"args.lock"}],"returns":[{"description":"A sha256 hex digest.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":200},"order":10,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:200","src":"src/cache.ts:244"},"level":0},{"id":"sweepDeclarations","longname":"sweepDeclarations","name":"sweepDeclarations","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Finds every `.d.ts` under the project roots (capped at {@link DTS_SWEEP_CAP}).","params":[{"description":"The resolved project source directories.","name":"srcDirs","type":{"names":["readonly string[]"]}},{"description":"The maximum number of declaration files to collect (default {@link DTS_SWEEP_CAP}).","name":"cap","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Absolute paths of declaration files, in stable sorted order.","type":{"names":["Promise<string[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":215},"order":11,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:215","src":"src/cache.ts:258"},"level":0},{"id":"toolchainFingerprint","longname":"toolchainFingerprint","name":"toolchainFingerprint","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Computes the cache fingerprint of the toolchain — everything about the\ninstalled mdocs + jsdoc + TypeScript that can shape the rendered output.","returns":[{"description":"A sha256 hex digest.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":234},"order":12,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:234","src":"src/cache.ts:276"},"level":0},{"id":"evict","longname":"evict","name":"evict","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Drops the least-valuable entries until only `cap` remain.","params":[{"description":"The entry map to trim in place.","name":"entries","type":{"names":["Map<string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: \"md\" | \"tdata\"; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record<string, unknown>[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: \"no-jsdoc\"; }>"]}},{"description":"How many entries to drop.","name":"overflow","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":246},"order":13,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:246","src":"src/cache.ts:290"},"level":0},{"id":"evictionClass","longname":"evictionClass","name":"evictionClass","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Eviction class: no-jsdoc skips first, then tdata, then full markdown.","params":[{"description":"The entry to classify.","name":"entry","type":{"names":["{ fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: \"md\" | \"tdata\"; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record<string, unknown>[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: \"no-jsdoc\"; }"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"0 for skips, 1 for tdata, 2 for markdown.","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":259},"order":14,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:259","src":"src/cache.ts:302"},"level":0},{"id":"hashFile","longname":"hashFile","name":"hashFile","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Sha256 hex of a file's contents, or `UNREADABLE` when it cannot be read.","params":[{"description":"The absolute path of the file to fingerprint.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The hex digest, or the `UNREADABLE` sentinel.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":269},"async":true,"order":15,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:269","src":"src/cache.ts:312"},"level":0},{"id":"packageVersionOf","longname":"packageVersionOf","name":"packageVersionOf","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Version of an installed package, walking up from its entry point; `?` on failure.","params":[{"description":"The package name to look up.","name":"name","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The package version, or `?` when it cannot be resolved.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":283},"order":16,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:283","src":"src/cache.ts:326"},"level":0},{"id":"readManifest","longname":"readManifest","name":"readManifest","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads one `package.json`, returning its version when it names `name`.","params":[{"description":"Absolute path of the candidate manifest.","name":"manifestPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The expected package name.","name":"name","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The package version, or `undefined` when the file is unusable.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":311},"order":17,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:311","src":"src/cache.ts:352"},"level":0},{"id":"sha256","longname":"sha256","name":"sha256","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Sha256 hex digest of `text`.","params":[{"description":"The string or buffer to hash.","name":"text"}],"returns":[{"description":"The lowercase hex digest.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":329},"order":18,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/cache.js:329","src":"src/cache.ts:369"},"level":0}],"fp":"303be2a33c4b6cda71c91a203626097a508c2e6b0a174bde3284947bd1d7dbd5","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318418,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/config.test.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"be6efbbc922e6ae87e3b72a45d11e9a9b39f78cc13736a14bdae58a977d097cf","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318419,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/errors.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"MdocsError","longname":"MdocsError","name":"MdocsError","kind":"class","scope":"global","description":"Shared error type for all expected `mdocs` failures.\n\nEvery failure an average user can plausibly fix (bad config, missing\ndirectories, unreadable source files, …) is reported as a `MdocsError`\nwith a stable machine-readable `code`. Unexpected\nprogramming errors are left as plain `Error`s so they surface with a stack\ntrace instead of being masked by a friendly message.\n\nCodes (all stable, all thrown by the pipeline in one place):\n\n| Code | Thrown by | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `INVALID_CONFIG` | `schema.ts` / `config.ts` | Config fails zod validation (or a config exports a non-plain-object) |\n| `CONFIG_NOT_FOUND` | `config.ts` | Explicit `--config` path does not exist / is unreadable |\n| `CONFIG_LOAD_FAILED` | `config.ts` | Config module threw, rejected, or used unsupported syntax |\n| `NO_ROOTS` | `resolve.ts` | A `rootSrcDir` glob matched no directories |\n| `INVALID_ROOT` | `resolve.ts` | A resolved root is not a readable directory |\n| `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS` | `resolve.ts` | One root is nested inside another |\n| `OUTPUT_COLLISION` | `resolve.ts` | Two files would write the same `.md` |\n| `RENDER_TIMEOUT` | `render.ts` | jsdoc exceeded the per-file timeout |\n\nErrors are stringified into `RunResult.failed[].error` / `RenderFileResult.error`\nfor per-file failures, and thrown for run-fatal ones (`INVALID_CONFIG`,\n`CONFIG_*`, `NO_ROOTS`, `INVALID_ROOT`, `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS`, `OUTPUT_COLLISION`).","meta":{"lineno":27},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/errors.js:27","src":"src/errors.ts:27"},"level":0},{"id":"errorMessage","longname":"errorMessage","name":"errorMessage","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Stringifies an unknown caught value for diagnostics.","params":[{"description":"The caught value (Error, string, number, …).","name":"cause","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The error message, or the stringified value for non-Errors.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":41},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/errors.js:41","src":"src/errors.ts:43"},"level":0},{"id":"isMdocsError","longname":"isMdocsError","name":"isMdocsError","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Narrows `error` to `MdocsError`.","params":[{"description":"The value to narrow.","name":"error","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` when `error` is a `MdocsError`.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":49},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/errors.js:49","src":"src/errors.ts:52"},"level":0},{"id":"MdocsError#code","longname":"MdocsError#code","name":"code","kind":"member","scope":"instance","description":"Stable machine-readable code, e.g. `CONFIG_NOT_FOUND`, `NO_ROOTS`, `INVALID_CONFIG`.","memberof":"MdocsError","meta":{"lineno":29},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/errors.js:29","src":"src/errors.ts:29"},"level":0}],"fp":"4d7a57cdeb9a8946302e3728fdd80ff21f1e416f0a7b578a305d15327468c4b2","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318421,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/lines.test.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"8268728562b3e97aa55bef02dfe71db70d60de0b6bd5ccd2acec68d0506e7b02","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318422,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/lines.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"nullMapper","longname":"nullMapper","name":"nullMapper","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"A mapper whose lookups always fail — used when the map is unusable.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":191},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:191","src":"src/lines.ts:202"},"level":0},{"id":"createLineMapper","longname":"createLineMapper","name":"createLineMapper","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds a line mapper from a sourcemap JSON string.","params":[{"description":"Raw `*.js.map` / inline sourcemap JSON.","name":"mapJson","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Location of the map, used to resolve relative `sources`.","name":"mapUrl","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Optional absolute path of the original source file.\n  When set, the map must reference it; otherwise the map is considered\n  stale or unrelated and every lookup returns `null` — the caller can\n  then fall back to an approximation instead of publishing misleading\n  line numbers.","name":"expectSource","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The line mapper.","type":{"names":["SourceLineMapper"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":33},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:33","src":"src/lines.ts:48"},"level":0},{"id":"readFileSourceMap","longname":"readFileSourceMap","name":"readFileSourceMap","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads the sourcemap for a generated `.js` file. The sibling `<file>.js.map`\nis the cheap common case and is tried first; only if it is absent do we\ntouch the (potentially large) `.js` file to look for an inline map, and\nthen only its tail.","params":[{"description":"Absolute path of the generated `.js` file.","name":"jsAbsPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Which map is available (`map` / `no-map` / `no-dist`).","type":{"names":["Promise<DistMapInfo>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":92},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:92","src":"src/lines.ts:107"},"level":0},{"id":"extractInlineMap","longname":"extractInlineMap","name":"extractInlineMap","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Extracts and decodes a base64 inline sourcemap, if present.","params":[{"description":"The `.js` source text (only the tail is examined).","name":"source","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The decoded map JSON, or `null` when no usable inline map exists.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":142},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:142","src":"src/lines.ts:155"},"level":0},{"id":"normalizeSource","longname":"normalizeSource","name":"normalizeSource","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Normalizes a resolved source entry or an absolute path for comparison.\nFile URLs (what `resolve-uri` produces on Windows) are decoded to native\npaths; separators are unified and trailing slashes trimmed. Comparison is\ncase-insensitive on Windows only.","params":[{"description":"The absolute path or file URL to normalize.","name":"source","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The normalized path (posix separators, no trailing slash).","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":165},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:165","src":"src/lines.ts:176"},"level":0},{"id":"tryFileURLToPath","longname":"tryFileURLToPath","name":"tryFileURLToPath","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Converts a `file:` URL to a filesystem path.","params":[{"description":"The string to convert.","name":"source","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The decoded path, or `source` unchanged when it is not a file URL.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":181},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/lines.js:181","src":"src/lines.ts:192"},"level":0}],"fp":"c1768d5d058a0db78deb020a0be560ac1d5c91a50428b169b012626f820ea736","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318423,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/pool.test.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"bafc8f2a2e8ae4d888f5597a6fe1a34e5315d35e8bb31d0d6701a29f97114c81","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318424,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/pool.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"mapPool","longname":"mapPool","name":"mapPool","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Maps `items` through `fn` with at most `limit` promises in flight, preserving\ninput order in the results array.\n\n`fn` is expected to handle its own errors (e.g. by returning a result object\ninstead of throwing) when the caller wants per-item failure collection rather\nthan abort-on-first-error semantics. If `fn` throws, the whole batch is\nabandoned: remaining items never run and results are discarded.","params":[{"description":"The work items, read in order.","name":"items","type":{"names":["readonly T[]"]}},{"description":"Maximum number of concurrent `fn` invocations.","name":"limit","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"The async task applied to each item.","name":"fn","type":{"names":["(item: T, index: number) => Promise<R>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The task results, in the same order as `items`.","type":{"names":["Promise<R[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":14},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/pool.js:14","src":"src/pool.ts:14"},"level":0}],"fp":"21c62f0b42dbcd1517a5221dd2736ff1704121a85eb991082dbcca49fb911406","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318424,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/resolve.test.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"tmpCopy","longname":"tmpCopy","name":"tmpCopy","kind":"function","scope":"global","params":[{"description":"The fixture repo name to copy.","name":"src","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute path of the copied project.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":18},"async":true,"order":0,"mdocs":{"src":"src/resolve.test.ts:21"},"level":0}],"fp":"0477e43c57868833b5133a45bcf364e57c073c92fc9445a74d7e65d94ab50d6b","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318425,"symbols":0},"md:src/cli.ts":{"fp":"6fed0362c0f0ffc6ffd6e258a9f65519f4f0a52cdaba4d2cb1e37a2dd21cfb80","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#execute\">execute(roots, options)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;number&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs the pipeline and prints the summary. Returns the exit code.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatUnexpected\">formatUnexpected(error)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Formats an unexpected error, honoring MDOCS_DEBUG for stack traces.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseParallelism\">parseParallelism(value)</a> ⇒ <code>number | boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Parses <code>--parallelism</code> into true | false | integer. Range checks live in the config schema.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#printSummary\">printSummary(result, verbose)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Prints the one-line summary and the failures, if any.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#printVerbose\">printVerbose(result)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Prints resolved settings and per-file details (--verbose).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"execute\"></a>\n\n## execute(roots, options) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;number&gt;</code>\nRuns the pipeline and prints the summary. Returns the exit code.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;number&gt;</code> - The process exit code (`0` ok / dry-run, `1` on failure).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| roots | <code>string[]</code> | Positional `rootSrcDir` arguments from the CLI. |\n| options | <code>CliOptions</code> | Parsed CLI flags. |\n\nsrc: src/cli.ts:71  \ndist: dist/cli.js:49\n<a name=\"formatUnexpected\"></a>\n\n## formatUnexpected(error) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFormats an unexpected error, honoring MDOCS_DEBUG for stack traces.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The message (plus stack trace when `MDOCS_DEBUG` is set).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error | <code>unknown</code> | The unexpected error to format. |\n\nsrc: src/cli.ts:110  \ndist: dist/cli.js:93\n<a name=\"parseParallelism\"></a>\n\n## parseParallelism(value) ⇒ <code>number \\| boolean</code>\nParses `--parallelism` into true | false | integer. Range checks live in the config schema.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>number \\| boolean</code> - `true`, `false`, or the parsed integer.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>string</code> | The raw flag value. |\n\nsrc: src/cli.ts:121  \ndist: dist/cli.js:105\n<a name=\"printSummary\"></a>\n\n## printSummary(result, verbose)\nPrints the one-line summary and the failures, if any.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| result | <code>RunResult</code> | The run result to summarize. |\n| verbose | <code>boolean</code> | When set, already printed in `printVerbose`; controls the dry-run listing. |\n\nsrc: src/cli.ts:136  \ndist: dist/cli.js:121\n<a name=\"printVerbose\"></a>\n\n## printVerbose(result)\nPrints resolved settings and per-file details (--verbose).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| result | <code>RunResult</code> | The run result to print. |\n\nsrc: src/cli.ts:162  \ndist: dist/cli.js:150\n","symbols":5},"md:src/config.test.ts":{"fp":"7b55a740bbac147dc32e2e82f7b8778791666691575621db8d34fca1720c53e1","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0},"md:src/lines.test.ts":{"fp":"ae148a07377905d38aa375b6459e9d8a7aed00abd6111d2827dfeecf8e4f17c3","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0},"md:src/pool.test.ts":{"fp":"a7621f4a42f2602ad39e134892a102a4e611a782810610da2cd90f8bdc20386c","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0},"md:src/config.ts":{"fp":"31ab2909845f22d50819dc160fa5f83ca54cad348dd122af9d9943c3a35b4a44","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#defineConfig\">defineConfig(config)</a> ⇒ <code>MdocsConfigExport</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Identity helper for typed configs, mirroring vite&#39;s <code>defineConfig</code>:\n<code>export default defineConfig({ … })</code>. Purely an authoring aid — validation\nhappens in <code>resolveConfig</code>, after the config is loaded.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#loadConfig\">loadConfig(cwd, explicitPath, overrides)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ config: ResolvedMdocsConfig; filePath: string | undefined; }&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Locates, loads, evaluates and validates the config file for <code>cwd</code>.</p>\n<p>When no config file exists and no explicit path was given, the run falls\nback to the default configuration (vite behavior) and <code>filePath</code> is\n<code>undefined</code>. An explicit <code>--config</code> path that does not exist always\nthrows.</p>\n<p><code>overrides</code> (config keys provided out-of-band, e.g. CLI flags or a\nprogrammatic call) are merged over the file&#39;s config — an override always\nwins for its own key, everything else comes from the file.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#resolveConfig\">resolveConfig(raw)</a> ⇒ <code>ResolvedMdocsConfig</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Resolves and validates a user-facing config into a <code>ResolvedMdocsConfig</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#configLoadError\">configLoadError(filePath, cause)</a> ⇒ <code>MdocsError</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Wraps config-loading failures with a consistent code and message.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#definedOverrides\">definedOverrides(overrides)</a> ⇒ <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Keeps only the keys of <code>overrides</code> that are actually set.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#describeType\">describeType(value)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Human-readable description of a value&#39;s runtime type.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#evaluateConfigExport\">evaluateConfigExport(exported, filePath)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Resolves the exported value, calling the function form if present.\nPromise exports are resolved transparently: <code>await</code> assimilates thenables,\nso by the time the value gets here any promise layers have already settled.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#importConfigModule\">importConfigModule(filePath)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Imports a config module, choosing the loader the same way vite and Node do:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>file</th>\n<th>loader</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>.mjs</code></td>\n<td>ESM always</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>.cjs</code></td>\n<td><code>require</code> (never silently reinterpreted)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>.js</code> + <code>&quot;type&quot;: &quot;module&quot;</code></td>\n<td>ESM always</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>.js</code> + <code>&quot;type&quot;: &quot;commonjs&quot;</code> or no <code>package.json</code></td>\n<td><code>require</code> first,</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>falling back to a sibling <code>.mjs</code> copy only for ESM-in-CJS</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>require()</code> of an ESM <code>.js</code> file fails with a plain <code>SyntaxError</code> on current\nNode versions, so <code>.js</code> ESM configs in <code>&quot;type&quot;: &quot;commonjs&quot;</code> packages load\nthrough the fallback, not through <code>require(esm)</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#importEsmInCommonJsPackage\">importEsmInCommonJsPackage(filePath)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Imports ESM config living in a <code>.js</code> file of a CommonJS-typed package.\nThe copy is written <strong>next to the config file</strong> — so relative imports in\nthe config keep working — with a hidden, unique name, removed afterwards.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isEsmInCjsError\">isEsmInCjsError(error)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>True when <code>error</code> reports ESM syntax loaded as CommonJS (Node-version-dependent).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isModuleNamespace\">isModuleNamespace(value)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Detects a native ESM module namespace exotic object.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#locateConfigFile\">locateConfigFile(cwd, explicitPath)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Finds the config file to use, honoring an explicit <code>--config</code> override.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#nearestPackageType\">nearestPackageType(filePath)</a> ⇒ <code>&quot;commonjs&quot; | &quot;module&quot;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Nearest <code>package.json</code> <code>&quot;type&quot;</code> walking up from <code>filePath</code> (or undefined).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#resolveParallelism\">resolveParallelism(value)</a> ⇒ <code>number</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Resolves the effective worker count (&quot;true&quot; = all cores).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"defineConfig\"></a>\n\n## defineConfig(config) ⇒ <code>MdocsConfigExport</code>\nIdentity helper for typed configs, mirroring vite's `defineConfig`:\n`export default defineConfig({ … })`. Purely an authoring aid — validation\nhappens in `resolveConfig`, after the config is loaded.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>MdocsConfigExport</code> - The config export, unchanged.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| config | <code>MdocsConfigExport</code> | The typed config object, function, or promise of either. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:80  \ndist: dist/config.js:38\n<a name=\"loadConfig\"></a>\n\n## loadConfig(cwd, explicitPath, overrides) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;{ config: ResolvedMdocsConfig; filePath: string \\| undefined; }&gt;</code>\nLocates, loads, evaluates and validates the config file for `cwd`.\n\nWhen no config file exists and no explicit path was given, the run falls\nback to the default configuration (vite behavior) and `filePath` is\n`undefined`. An explicit `--config` path that does not exist always\nthrows.\n\n`overrides` (config keys provided out-of-band, e.g. CLI flags or a\nprogrammatic call) are merged over the file's config — an override always\nwins for its own key, everything else comes from the file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;{ config: ResolvedMdocsConfig; filePath: string \\| undefined; }&gt;</code> - The resolved config and the file (if any) it came from.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cwd | <code>string</code> | Working directory for config lookup and relative roots. |\n| explicitPath | <code>string</code> | Explicit `--config` path (beats auto-discovery). |\n| overrides | <code>{ cache?: boolean; cachePath?: string; outDirName?: string; parallelism?: number \\| boolean; rootDistDir?: string; rootSrcDir?: string \\| string[]; }</code> | Config keys merged over the file's config. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:102  \ndist: dist/config.js:58\n<a name=\"resolveConfig\"></a>\n\n## resolveConfig(raw) ⇒ <code>ResolvedMdocsConfig</code>\nResolves and validates a user-facing config into a `ResolvedMdocsConfig`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>ResolvedMdocsConfig</code> - The frozen, fully-resolved config.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| raw | <code>unknown</code> | The user-facing (unvalidated) config. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:131  \ndist: dist/config.js:85\n<a name=\"configLoadError\"></a>\n\n## configLoadError(filePath, cause) ⇒ <code>MdocsError</code>\nWraps config-loading failures with a consistent code and message.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>MdocsError</code> - A `MdocsError` with code `CONFIG_LOAD_FAILED`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| filePath | <code>string</code> | The config file that failed to load. |\n| cause | <code>unknown</code> | The underlying error. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:150  \ndist: dist/config.js:103\n<a name=\"definedOverrides\"></a>\n\n## definedOverrides(overrides) ⇒ <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code>\nKeeps only the keys of `overrides` that are actually set.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;</code> - The overrides with only the set keys.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| overrides | <code>{ cache?: boolean; cachePath?: string; outDirName?: string; parallelism?: number \\| boolean; rootDistDir?: string; rootSrcDir?: string \\| string[]; }</code> | The user-facing config overrides (any keys missing are kept unset). |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:160  \ndist: dist/config.js:112\n<a name=\"describeType\"></a>\n\n## describeType(value) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nHuman-readable description of a value's runtime type.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - `null`, `an array`, or the `typeof` string.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>unknown</code> | The value to describe. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:174  \ndist: dist/config.js:126\n<a name=\"evaluateConfigExport\"></a>\n\n## evaluateConfigExport(exported, filePath) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code>\nResolves the exported value, calling the function form if present.\nPromise exports are resolved transparently: `await` assimilates thenables,\nso by the time the value gets here any promise layers have already settled.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code> - The resolved plain-object config.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| exported | <code>unknown</code> | The raw module export to resolve. |\n| filePath | <code>string</code> | The config file it came from (for errors). |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:192  \ndist: dist/config.js:144\n<a name=\"importConfigModule\"></a>\n\n## importConfigModule(filePath) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code>\nImports a config module, choosing the loader the same way vite and Node do:\n\n| file        | loader                                                    |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.mjs`      | ESM always                                                |\n| `.cjs`      | `require` (never silently reinterpreted)                  |\n| `.js` + `\"type\": \"module\"`                       | ESM always        |\n| `.js` + `\"type\": \"commonjs\"` or no `package.json` | `require` first,  |\n|             | falling back to a sibling `.mjs` copy only for ESM-in-CJS |\n\n`require()` of an ESM `.js` file fails with a plain `SyntaxError` on current\nNode versions, so `.js` ESM configs in `\"type\": \"commonjs\"` packages load\nthrough the fallback, not through `require(esm)`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code> - The module export (namespace object for ESM, as-is for CJS).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| filePath | <code>string</code> | The config file to import. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:232  \ndist: dist/config.js:180\n<a name=\"importEsmInCommonJsPackage\"></a>\n\n## importEsmInCommonJsPackage(filePath) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code>\nImports ESM config living in a `.js` file of a CommonJS-typed package.\nThe copy is written **next to the config file** — so relative imports in\nthe config keep working — with a hidden, unique name, removed afterwards.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;unknown&gt;</code> - The module export.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| filePath | <code>string</code> | The `.js` config file whose ESM-in-CJS content is loaded. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:266  \ndist: dist/config.js:217\n<a name=\"isEsmInCjsError\"></a>\n\n## isEsmInCjsError(error) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nTrue when `error` reports ESM syntax loaded as CommonJS (Node-version-dependent).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - Whether the error is an ESM-in-CJS load failure.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error | <code>unknown</code> | The catch value to classify. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:290  \ndist: dist/config.js:238\n<a name=\"isModuleNamespace\"></a>\n\n## isModuleNamespace(value) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nDetects a native ESM module namespace exotic object.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` for a native ESM module namespace object.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>unknown</code> | The value to test. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:305  \ndist: dist/config.js:252\n<a name=\"locateConfigFile\"></a>\n\n## locateConfigFile(cwd, explicitPath) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nFinds the config file to use, honoring an explicit `--config` override.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The absolute path, or `undefined` when none exists and none was given.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cwd | <code>string</code> | Working directory to look up config files in. |\n| explicitPath | <code>string</code> | Explicit `--config` path (never auto-discovered). |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:315  \ndist: dist/config.js:261\n<a name=\"nearestPackageType\"></a>\n\n## nearestPackageType(filePath) ⇒ <code>&quot;commonjs&quot; \\| &quot;module&quot;</code>\nNearest `package.json` `\"type\"` walking up from `filePath` (or undefined).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>&quot;commonjs&quot; \\| &quot;module&quot;</code> - `module`, `commonjs`, or `undefined` when no nearest `package.json` declares it.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| filePath | <code>string</code> | The config file to start from. |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:344  \ndist: dist/config.js:290\n<a name=\"resolveParallelism\"></a>\n\n## resolveParallelism(value) ⇒ <code>number</code>\nResolves the effective worker count (\"true\" = all cores).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>number</code> - The concrete worker count.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>number \\| boolean</code> | The user-facing `parallelism` (boolean or number). |\n\nsrc: src/config.ts:366  \ndist: dist/config.js:314\n","symbols":14},"tdata:src/render.mocked.test.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"doclet","longname":"doclet","name":"doclet","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds a minimal doclet for tests (defaults: function/thing).","params":[{"description":"The jsdoc-reported line number of the doclet.","name":"lineno","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"The doclet kind.","name":"kind","defaultvalue":"function","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The doclet name.","name":"name","defaultvalue":"thing","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The doclet object.","type":{"names":["{ kind: string; longname: string; meta: { filename: string; lineno: number; path: string; }; name: string; params: { description: string; name: string; }[]; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":30},"order":0,"mdocs":{"src":"src/render.mocked.test.ts:36"},"level":0},{"id":"setup","longname":"setup","name":"setup","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Writes `files` (name → content) under `<dir>/src`.","params":[{"description":"The fixture root to create.","name":"dir","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The files to write.","name":"files","type":{"names":["Record<string, string>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Nothing.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":45},"async":true,"order":1,"mdocs":{"src":"src/render.mocked.test.ts:52"},"level":0},{"id":"sourceFile","longname":"sourceFile","name":"sourceFile","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds a SourceFile record for tests.","params":[{"description":"The posix-relative path of the source.","name":"relPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The source extension.","name":"extension","type":{"names":["\".js\" | \".jsx\" | \".mjs\" | \".cjs\" | \".ts\" | \".tsx\" | \".mts\" | \".cts\""]}},{"description":"The absolute project directory.","name":"dir","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The SourceFile record.","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":58},"order":2,"mdocs":{"src":"src/render.mocked.test.ts:66"},"level":0}],"fp":"f986855055220cd1a57e4386ba06c3a01d5382e8fb0b786b257ad3a770fe31c3","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816318698,"symbols":0},"md:src/resolve.test.ts":{"fp":"84c3a091bbb902fc166ccfabb687c138c1280b1eecf86d6ed7fd49fa0cb462f5","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"tmpCopy\"></a>\n\n## tmpCopy(src) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The absolute path of the copied project.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| src | <code>string</code> | The fixture repo name to copy. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.test.ts:21  \n","symbols":1},"md:src/cache.ts":{"fp":"c30cc0876e52cb978e326c44f9fbe056f18e59ba8055536291fa4c6127dec825","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES\">MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Keep in sync with the zod caps in <code>schema.js</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#MAX_DOCLETS\">MAX_DOCLETS</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Keep in sync with the zod cap in <code>schema.js</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#CACHE_FORMAT\">CACHE_FORMAT</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Cache format version — bump on incompatible entry changes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#CACHE_CAP\">CACHE_CAP</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Maximum entries kept; least-recently-used are evicted first.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#RENDER_FORMAT\">RENDER_FORMAT</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Distinguishes cache behavior across renderer/output-format changes.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#DTS_SWEEP_CAP\">DTS_SWEEP_CAP</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Cap on .d.ts declaration files swept into the program fingerprint.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#createCache\">createCache(options)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Cache&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Loads a cache from disk (never throws), returning a ready-to-use handle.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#distMaterialOf\">distMaterialOf(distJs)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>The dist-side fingerprint material for one file — hashes the dist map when\npresent, else a sentinel for its absence.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fileFingerprints\">fileFingerprints(args)</a> ⇒ <code>FileFingerprints</code></dt>\n<dd><p>The per-file fingerprints and tier keys for one source file.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#lockfileFingerprint\">lockfileFingerprint(cwd)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>The sha256 of the lockfile in <code>cwd</code>, or <code>undefined</code> when absent/unreadable.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#programFingerprint\">programFingerprint(args)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>The whole-program fingerprint for .ts files — every source and declaration\nfile under the project roots, plus the lockfile and the TypeScript version.\nCovers first-party <code>.d.ts</code> files that are imported but never roots.\nNode_modules trees behind a lockfile are pinned by the lockfile hash; trees\ndrifted from their lockfile (postinstall patches) can serve stale types.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#sweepDeclarations\">sweepDeclarations(srcDirs, cap)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Finds every <code>.d.ts</code> under the project roots (capped at <a href=\"#DTS_SWEEP_CAP\">DTS_SWEEP_CAP</a>).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#toolchainFingerprint\">toolchainFingerprint()</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Computes the cache fingerprint of the toolchain — everything about the\ninstalled mdocs + jsdoc + TypeScript that can shape the rendered output.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#evict\">evict(entries, overflow)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Drops the least-valuable entries until only <code>cap</code> remain.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#evictionClass\">evictionClass(entry)</a> ⇒ <code>number</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Eviction class: no-jsdoc skips first, then tdata, then full markdown.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#hashFile\">hashFile(path)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Sha256 hex of a file&#39;s contents, or <code>UNREADABLE</code> when it cannot be read.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#packageVersionOf\">packageVersionOf(name)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Version of an installed package, walking up from its entry point; <code>?</code> on failure.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readManifest\">readManifest(manifestPath, name)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads one <code>package.json</code>, returning its version when it names <code>name</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#sha256\">sha256(text)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Sha256 hex digest of <code>text</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"MAX_MARKDOWN_BYTES\"></a>\n\n## MAX\\_MARKDOWN\\_BYTES\nKeep in sync with the zod caps in `schema.js`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:49  \ndist: dist/cache.js:45\n<a name=\"MAX_DOCLETS\"></a>\n\n## MAX\\_DOCLETS\nKeep in sync with the zod cap in `schema.js`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:51  \ndist: dist/cache.js:47\n<a name=\"CACHE_FORMAT\"></a>\n\n## CACHE\\_FORMAT\nCache format version — bump on incompatible entry changes.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:54  \ndist: dist/cache.js:49\n<a name=\"CACHE_CAP\"></a>\n\n## CACHE\\_CAP\nMaximum entries kept; least-recently-used are evicted first.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:56  \ndist: dist/cache.js:51\n<a name=\"RENDER_FORMAT\"></a>\n\n## RENDER\\_FORMAT\nDistinguishes cache behavior across renderer/output-format changes.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:58  \ndist: dist/cache.js:53\n<a name=\"DTS_SWEEP_CAP\"></a>\n\n## DTS\\_SWEEP\\_CAP\nCap on .d.ts declaration files swept into the program fingerprint.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:60  \ndist: dist/cache.js:55\n<a name=\"createCache\"></a>\n\n## createCache(options) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Cache&gt;</code>\nLoads a cache from disk (never throws), returning a ready-to-use handle.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Cache&gt;</code> - The cache (issues carry any problems found at load time).  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| options | The cache location. |\n| options.path | Absolute path of the cache file. |\n| options.cap | Maximum entries (default [CACHE_CAP](#CACHE_CAP)). |\n| options.now | Clock override for tests (default [Date.now](Date.now)). |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:107  \ndist: dist/cache.js:64\n<a name=\"distMaterialOf\"></a>\n\n## distMaterialOf(distJs) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nThe dist-side fingerprint material for one file — hashes the dist map when\npresent, else a sentinel for its absence.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - `map:<sha256(mapJson)>` / `no-map` / `no-dist`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| distJs | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the expected dist `.js` file. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:168  \ndist: dist/cache.js:133\n<a name=\"fileFingerprints\"></a>\n\n## fileFingerprints(args) ⇒ <code>FileFingerprints</code>\nThe per-file fingerprints and tier keys for one source file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>FileFingerprints</code> - The fingerprints and both tier keys.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| args | The inputs to fingerprint. |\n| args.file | The source file. |\n| args.cwd | The run's working directory (cache keys are cwd-relative). |\n| args.file.absPath | The absolute path of the source file. |\n| args.file.extension | The source extension (e.g. `.ts`). |\n| args.srcText | The source text (already read by the caller). |\n| args.distMaterial | Dist-side material from [distMaterialOf](#distMaterialOf), or `null`. |\n| args.isTypeScript | Whether the file is `.ts`-family. |\n| args.programFp | [programFingerprint](#programFingerprint) of the run, or `null` for .js. |\n| args.toolchainFp | [toolchainFingerprint](#toolchainFingerprint) of the run. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:188  \ndist: dist/cache.js:153\n<a name=\"lockfileFingerprint\"></a>\n\n## lockfileFingerprint(cwd) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nThe sha256 of the lockfile in `cwd`, or `undefined` when absent/unreadable.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The lockfile digest.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cwd | <code>string</code> | The run's working directory. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:220  \ndist: dist/cache.js:176\n<a name=\"programFingerprint\"></a>\n\n## programFingerprint(args) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nThe whole-program fingerprint for .ts files — every source and declaration\nfile under the project roots, plus the lockfile and the TypeScript version.\nCovers first-party `.d.ts` files that are imported but never roots.\nNode_modules trees behind a lockfile are pinned by the lockfile hash; trees\ndrifted from their lockfile (postinstall patches) can serve stale types.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - A sha256 hex digest.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| args | The inputs to fingerprint. |\n| args.tsFiles | Absolute paths of every `.ts`-family file in the run (in any order). |\n| args.sweep | Absolute paths of every `.d.ts` under the project roots (in any order). |\n| args.lock | sha256 of the lockfile, or `undefined` when absent. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:244  \ndist: dist/cache.js:200\n<a name=\"sweepDeclarations\"></a>\n\n## sweepDeclarations(srcDirs, cap) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code>\nFinds every `.d.ts` under the project roots (capped at [DTS_SWEEP_CAP](#DTS_SWEEP_CAP)).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code> - Absolute paths of declaration files, in stable sorted order.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| srcDirs | <code>readonly string[]</code> | The resolved project source directories. |\n| cap | <code>number</code> | The maximum number of declaration files to collect (default [DTS_SWEEP_CAP](#DTS_SWEEP_CAP)). |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:258  \ndist: dist/cache.js:215\n<a name=\"toolchainFingerprint\"></a>\n\n## toolchainFingerprint() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nComputes the cache fingerprint of the toolchain — everything about the\ninstalled mdocs + jsdoc + TypeScript that can shape the rendered output.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - A sha256 hex digest.  \nsrc: src/cache.ts:276  \ndist: dist/cache.js:234\n<a name=\"evict\"></a>\n\n## evict(entries, overflow)\nDrops the least-valuable entries until only `cap` remain.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| entries | <code>Map&lt;string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; \\| &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }&gt;</code> | The entry map to trim in place. |\n| overflow | <code>number</code> | How many entries to drop. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:290  \ndist: dist/cache.js:246\n<a name=\"evictionClass\"></a>\n\n## evictionClass(entry) ⇒ <code>number</code>\nEviction class: no-jsdoc skips first, then tdata, then full markdown.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>number</code> - 0 for skips, 1 for tdata, 2 for markdown.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| entry | <code>{ fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; \\| &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }</code> | The entry to classify. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:302  \ndist: dist/cache.js:259\n<a name=\"hashFile\"></a>\n\n## hashFile(path) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nSha256 hex of a file's contents, or `UNREADABLE` when it cannot be read.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The hex digest, or the `UNREADABLE` sentinel.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The absolute path of the file to fingerprint. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:312  \ndist: dist/cache.js:269\n<a name=\"packageVersionOf\"></a>\n\n## packageVersionOf(name) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nVersion of an installed package, walking up from its entry point; `?` on failure.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The package version, or `?` when it cannot be resolved.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| name | <code>string</code> | The package name to look up. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:326  \ndist: dist/cache.js:283\n<a name=\"readManifest\"></a>\n\n## readManifest(manifestPath, name) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads one `package.json`, returning its version when it names `name`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The package version, or `undefined` when the file is unusable.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| manifestPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the candidate manifest. |\n| name | <code>string</code> | The expected package name. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:352  \ndist: dist/cache.js:311\n<a name=\"sha256\"></a>\n\n## sha256(text) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nSha256 hex digest of `text`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The lowercase hex digest.  \n\n| Param | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| text | The string or buffer to hash. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.ts:369  \ndist: dist/cache.js:329\n","symbols":19},"md:src/errors.ts":{"fp":"03fb5bb4c56640737b6a422c18ce3a4afa9eb633ff9b09f8e7b04369ca6053eb","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Classes\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#MdocsError\">MdocsError</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Shared error type for all expected <code>mdocs</code> failures.</p>\n<p>Every failure an average user can plausibly fix (bad config, missing\ndirectories, unreadable source files, …) is reported as a <code>MdocsError</code>\nwith a stable machine-readable <code>code</code>. Unexpected\nprogramming errors are left as plain <code>Error</code>s so they surface with a stack\ntrace instead of being masked by a friendly message.</p>\n<p>Codes (all stable, all thrown by the pipeline in one place):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Code</th>\n<th>Thrown by</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>INVALID_CONFIG</code></td>\n<td><code>schema.ts</code> / <code>config.ts</code></td>\n<td>Config fails zod validation (or a config exports a non-plain-object)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CONFIG_NOT_FOUND</code></td>\n<td><code>config.ts</code></td>\n<td>Explicit <code>--config</code> path does not exist / is unreadable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>CONFIG_LOAD_FAILED</code></td>\n<td><code>config.ts</code></td>\n<td>Config module threw, rejected, or used unsupported syntax</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>NO_ROOTS</code></td>\n<td><code>resolve.ts</code></td>\n<td>A <code>rootSrcDir</code> glob matched no directories</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>INVALID_ROOT</code></td>\n<td><code>resolve.ts</code></td>\n<td>A resolved root is not a readable directory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OVERLAPPING_ROOTS</code></td>\n<td><code>resolve.ts</code></td>\n<td>One root is nested inside another</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>OUTPUT_COLLISION</code></td>\n<td><code>resolve.ts</code></td>\n<td>Two files would write the same <code>.md</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>RENDER_TIMEOUT</code></td>\n<td><code>render.ts</code></td>\n<td>jsdoc exceeded the per-file timeout</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Errors are stringified into <code>RunResult.failed[].error</code> / <code>RenderFileResult.error</code>\nfor per-file failures, and thrown for run-fatal ones (<code>INVALID_CONFIG</code>,\n<code>CONFIG_*</code>, <code>NO_ROOTS</code>, <code>INVALID_ROOT</code>, <code>OVERLAPPING_ROOTS</code>, <code>OUTPUT_COLLISION</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#errorMessage\">errorMessage(cause)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Stringifies an unknown caught value for diagnostics.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isMdocsError\">isMdocsError(error)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Narrows <code>error</code> to <code>MdocsError</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"MdocsError\"></a>\n\n## MdocsError\nShared error type for all expected `mdocs` failures.\n\nEvery failure an average user can plausibly fix (bad config, missing\ndirectories, unreadable source files, …) is reported as a `MdocsError`\nwith a stable machine-readable `code`. Unexpected\nprogramming errors are left as plain `Error`s so they surface with a stack\ntrace instead of being masked by a friendly message.\n\nCodes (all stable, all thrown by the pipeline in one place):\n\n| Code | Thrown by | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `INVALID_CONFIG` | `schema.ts` / `config.ts` | Config fails zod validation (or a config exports a non-plain-object) |\n| `CONFIG_NOT_FOUND` | `config.ts` | Explicit `--config` path does not exist / is unreadable |\n| `CONFIG_LOAD_FAILED` | `config.ts` | Config module threw, rejected, or used unsupported syntax |\n| `NO_ROOTS` | `resolve.ts` | A `rootSrcDir` glob matched no directories |\n| `INVALID_ROOT` | `resolve.ts` | A resolved root is not a readable directory |\n| `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS` | `resolve.ts` | One root is nested inside another |\n| `OUTPUT_COLLISION` | `resolve.ts` | Two files would write the same `.md` |\n| `RENDER_TIMEOUT` | `render.ts` | jsdoc exceeded the per-file timeout |\n\nErrors are stringified into `RunResult.failed[].error` / `RenderFileResult.error`\nfor per-file failures, and thrown for run-fatal ones (`INVALID_CONFIG`,\n`CONFIG_*`, `NO_ROOTS`, `INVALID_ROOT`, `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS`, `OUTPUT_COLLISION`).\n\n**Kind**: global class  \nsrc: src/errors.ts:27  \ndist: dist/errors.js:27\n<a name=\"MdocsError+code\"></a>\n\n### mdocsError.code\nStable machine-readable code, e.g. `CONFIG_NOT_FOUND`, `NO_ROOTS`, `INVALID_CONFIG`.\n\n**Kind**: instance property of [<code>MdocsError</code>](#MdocsError)  \nsrc: src/errors.ts:29  \ndist: dist/errors.js:29\n<a name=\"errorMessage\"></a>\n\n## errorMessage(cause) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nStringifies an unknown caught value for diagnostics.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The error message, or the stringified value for non-Errors.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cause | <code>unknown</code> | The caught value (Error, string, number, …). |\n\nsrc: src/errors.ts:43  \ndist: dist/errors.js:41\n<a name=\"isMdocsError\"></a>\n\n## isMdocsError(error) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nNarrows `error` to `MdocsError`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` when `error` is a `MdocsError`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error | <code>unknown</code> | The value to narrow. |\n\nsrc: src/errors.ts:52  \ndist: dist/errors.js:49\n","symbols":4},"md:src/lines.ts":{"fp":"4bef16fcb65582f79f392a43c7ed115fc311083cdc31cbb8dbf862f6396d495a","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#nullMapper\">nullMapper</a></dt>\n<dd><p>A mapper whose lookups always fail — used when the map is unusable.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#createLineMapper\">createLineMapper(mapJson, mapUrl, expectSource)</a> ⇒ <code>SourceLineMapper</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds a line mapper from a sourcemap JSON string.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readFileSourceMap\">readFileSourceMap(jsAbsPath)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DistMapInfo&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reads the sourcemap for a generated <code>.js</code> file. The sibling <code>&lt;file&gt;.js.map</code>\nis the cheap common case and is tried first; only if it is absent do we\ntouch the (potentially large) <code>.js</code> file to look for an inline map, and\nthen only its tail.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#extractInlineMap\">extractInlineMap(source)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Extracts and decodes a base64 inline sourcemap, if present.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#normalizeSource\">normalizeSource(source)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalizes a resolved source entry or an absolute path for comparison.\nFile URLs (what <code>resolve-uri</code> produces on Windows) are decoded to native\npaths; separators are unified and trailing slashes trimmed. Comparison is\ncase-insensitive on Windows only.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#tryFileURLToPath\">tryFileURLToPath(source)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Converts a <code>file:</code> URL to a filesystem path.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"nullMapper\"></a>\n\n## nullMapper\nA mapper whose lookups always fail — used when the map is unusable.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/lines.ts:202  \ndist: dist/lines.js:191\n<a name=\"createLineMapper\"></a>\n\n## createLineMapper(mapJson, mapUrl, expectSource) ⇒ <code>SourceLineMapper</code>\nBuilds a line mapper from a sourcemap JSON string.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>SourceLineMapper</code> - The line mapper.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| mapJson | <code>string</code> | Raw `*.js.map` / inline sourcemap JSON. |\n| mapUrl | <code>string</code> | Location of the map, used to resolve relative `sources`. |\n| expectSource | <code>string</code> | Optional absolute path of the original source file.   When set, the map must reference it; otherwise the map is considered   stale or unrelated and every lookup returns `null` — the caller can   then fall back to an approximation instead of publishing misleading   line numbers. |\n\nsrc: src/lines.ts:48  \ndist: dist/lines.js:33\n<a name=\"readFileSourceMap\"></a>\n\n## readFileSourceMap(jsAbsPath) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DistMapInfo&gt;</code>\nReads the sourcemap for a generated `.js` file. The sibling `<file>.js.map`\nis the cheap common case and is tried first; only if it is absent do we\ntouch the (potentially large) `.js` file to look for an inline map, and\nthen only its tail.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;DistMapInfo&gt;</code> - Which map is available (`map` / `no-map` / `no-dist`).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| jsAbsPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the generated `.js` file. |\n\nsrc: src/lines.ts:107  \ndist: dist/lines.js:92\n<a name=\"extractInlineMap\"></a>\n\n## extractInlineMap(source) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nExtracts and decodes a base64 inline sourcemap, if present.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The decoded map JSON, or `null` when no usable inline map exists.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| source | <code>string</code> | The `.js` source text (only the tail is examined). |\n\nsrc: src/lines.ts:155  \ndist: dist/lines.js:142\n<a name=\"normalizeSource\"></a>\n\n## normalizeSource(source) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nNormalizes a resolved source entry or an absolute path for comparison.\nFile URLs (what `resolve-uri` produces on Windows) are decoded to native\npaths; separators are unified and trailing slashes trimmed. Comparison is\ncase-insensitive on Windows only.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The normalized path (posix separators, no trailing slash).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| source | <code>string</code> | The absolute path or file URL to normalize. |\n\nsrc: src/lines.ts:176  \ndist: dist/lines.js:165\n<a name=\"tryFileURLToPath\"></a>\n\n## tryFileURLToPath(source) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nConverts a `file:` URL to a filesystem path.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The decoded path, or `source` unchanged when it is not a file URL.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| source | <code>string</code> | The string to convert. |\n\nsrc: src/lines.ts:192  \ndist: dist/lines.js:181\n","symbols":6},"md:src/pool.ts":{"fp":"b0af310126d00d38eb28a0d53ae07d54012a7072f756464bdc54c4ac3dfe0c3d","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"mapPool\"></a>\n\n## mapPool(items, limit, fn) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;R[]&gt;</code>\nMaps `items` through `fn` with at most `limit` promises in flight, preserving\ninput order in the results array.\n\n`fn` is expected to handle its own errors (e.g. by returning a result object\ninstead of throwing) when the caller wants per-item failure collection rather\nthan abort-on-first-error semantics. If `fn` throws, the whole batch is\nabandoned: remaining items never run and results are discarded.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;R[]&gt;</code> - The task results, in the same order as `items`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| items | <code>readonly T[]</code> | The work items, read in order. |\n| limit | <code>number</code> | Maximum number of concurrent `fn` invocations. |\n| fn | <code>(item: T, index: number) &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;R&gt;</code> | The async task applied to each item. |\n\nsrc: src/pool.ts:14  \ndist: dist/pool.js:14\n","symbols":1},"tdata:src/cache.test.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"tmpdirOf","longname":"tmpdirOf","name":"tmpdirOf","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Creates a self-cleaning temp directory.","params":[{"description":"The mkdtemp prefix to use.","name":"prefix","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute path of the created directory.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":18},"async":true,"order":0,"mdocs":{"src":"src/cache.test.ts:21"},"level":0}],"fp":"a09df6e3beded4b51e8a43d04c6b98518a6a0e578112852ad4c177ccb1cb7d14","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319245,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/doclet.test.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"656b8e295e7ef07b398b6b43bdc8bdffb700deff0799eae9bbfdfdfe4e1b3c43","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319248,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/render.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"DOCS_OVERRIDE","longname":"DOCS_OVERRIDE","name":"DOCS_OVERRIDE","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"The two handlebars partials injected into dmd.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":40},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:40","src":"src/render.ts:69"},"level":0},{"id":"DIST_EXTENSION","longname":"DIST_EXTENSION","name":"DIST_EXTENSION","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Dist extensions that differ from `source.slice(1)` (everything else strips the dot).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":319},"order":9,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:319","src":"src/render.ts:405"},"level":0},{"id":"renderSourceFile","longname":"renderSourceFile","name":"renderSourceFile","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Renders one source file into markdown (or reports why it could not).","params":[{"description":"The file to render and its pool index.","name":"job","type":{"names":["RenderFileJob"]}},{"description":"Render-time dependencies (scratch dir, partials, output path, TS program, pointer base, jsdoc timeout).","name":"deps","type":{"names":["{ cache?: Cache; fingerprints?: ReadonlyMap<string, FileFingerprints>; missingDistDirs?: ReadonlySet<string>; outPath: string; partials: readonly string[]; pointerBase: string; scratchDir: string; timeoutMs?: number; typeProgram: null | TypeProgram; }"]}},{"description":"A loaded cache (absent ⇒ cache disabled).","name":"deps.cache"},{"description":"The per-file cache fingerprints (absent ⇒ cache disabled).","name":"deps.fingerprints"},{"description":"Absolute distDirs known to be missing/not-directories (probed once per project by the run); for those projects no `dist:` line is emitted.","name":"deps.missingDistDirs"},{"description":"Per-file scratch directory for the transpiled/copied source.","name":"deps.scratchDir"},{"description":"The handlebars partial override files (dmd template).","name":"deps.partials"},{"description":"Where the generated markdown goes.","name":"deps.outPath"},{"description":"The project's TS program for checker types (null for JS files).","name":"deps.typeProgram"},{"description":"Absolute base for cwd-relative `src:`/`dist:` pointers.","name":"deps.pointerBase"},{"description":"jsdoc render timeout in milliseconds.","name":"deps.timeoutMs"}],"returns":[{"description":"The render outcome (markdown, skip or failure) — always resolves.","type":{"names":["Promise<RenderFileResult>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":66},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:66","src":"src/render.ts:101"},"level":0},{"id":"writeTemplatePartials","longname":"writeTemplatePartials","name":"writeTemplatePartials","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Writes the two injected partials into the run's scratch directory.","params":[{"description":"Scratch directory that will hold `partials/`.","name":"scratchDir","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute paths of the written partial files.","type":{"names":["Promise<string[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":128},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:128","src":"src/render.ts:194"},"level":0},{"id":"computePointers","longname":"computePointers","name":"computePointers","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Computes the per-doclet src/dist pointer map, keyed by generated line","params":[{"description":"The source file being rendered.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}},{"description":"The doclets to annotate (already normalized).","name":"data","type":{"names":["readonly DmdDoclet[]"]}},{"description":"Mapper from the in-memory transpile, or `null` for pass-through copies.","name":"transpileMapper","type":{"names":["SourceLineMapper"]}},{"description":"Per-file notes accumulator.","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}},{"description":"Absolute base for cwd-relative `src:`/`dist:` pointers.","name":"pointerBase","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"`true` when the project's dist folder was probed missing; the dist lookup is skipped entirely.","name":"distFolderMissing","defaultvalue":false,"type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A generated-line → pointer map.","type":{"names":["Promise<Map<number, SymbolPointer>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":149},"async":true,"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:149","src":"src/render.ts:216"},"level":0},{"id":"fetchTemplateData","longname":"fetchTemplateData","name":"fetchTemplateData","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Fetches template data for one file, reusing the tier-2 cache when possible.\nA cache hit skips the jsdoc child process; everything else (normalize,\npointer injection, checker types, render) still runs fresh.","params":[{"description":"The transpiled/copied source inside the scratch dir.","name":"scratchFile","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The render deps (may carry a `cache` and per-file `fingerprints`).","name":"deps","type":{"names":["{ cache?: Cache; fingerprints?: ReadonlyMap<string, FileFingerprints>; }"]}},{"description":"The loaded cache, or absent when caching is disabled.","name":"deps.cache"},{"description":"The per-file fingerprints, or absent when caching is disabled.","name":"deps.fingerprints"},{"description":"The source file being rendered.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}},{"description":"The jsdoc render timeout in milliseconds.","name":"timeoutMs","type":{"names":["number"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The normalized doclets.","type":{"names":["Promise<DmdDoclet[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":180},"async":true,"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:180","src":"src/render.ts:255"},"level":0},{"id":"pointerPath","longname":"pointerPath","name":"pointerPath","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Renders an absolute path relative to the workspace root, posix-style.","params":[{"description":"The absolute base the returned path is relative to.","name":"base","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The absolute path to render.","name":"absPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The posix-style relative path.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":213},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:213","src":"src/render.ts:295"},"level":0},{"id":"prepareForJsdoc","longname":"prepareForJsdoc","name":"prepareForJsdoc","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Transpiles (.ts family) or copies (.js family) the source for jsdoc.","params":[{"description":"The source file being prepared.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}},{"description":"The source text.","name":"srcText","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Per-file scratch directory to write into.","name":"scratchDir","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The prepared scratch file (or the transpile error).","type":{"names":["Promise<PreparedFile>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":223},"async":true,"order":6,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:223","src":"src/render.ts:306"},"level":0},{"id":"resolveDistPointer","longname":"resolveDistPointer","name":"resolveDistPointer","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Computes the dist pointer for one doclet. A missing dist folder (project probe)\nor dist file (per-file probe) omits the dist line entirely; when the dist map\nexists but the lookup misses, one \"dist sourcemap missing or unmatched\" note is\nrecorded instead.","params":[{"description":"The source (original) line for the symbol.","name":"srcLine","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"Mapper from the transpile emit, or `null` for pass-through copies.","name":"transpileMapper","type":{"names":["SourceLineMapper"]}},{"description":"Dist lookup context (kind, mapper, pointer path) computed once per file.","name":"dist","type":{"names":["DistPointerContext"]}},{"description":"Per-file notes accumulator.","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The `dist:` pointer line, or `undefined` when the dist line must be omitted.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":291},"order":7,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:291","src":"src/render.ts:373"},"level":0},{"id":"resolveSrcLine","longname":"resolveSrcLine","name":"resolveSrcLine","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Maps a doclet's generated line back to the original source line.","params":[{"description":"The jsdoc-reported line in the generated file.","name":"generatedLine","type":{"names":["number"]}},{"description":"Mapper from the transpile emit, or `null` for pass-through copies.","name":"transpileMapper","type":{"names":["SourceLineMapper"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The source line and whether it is approximate.","type":{"names":["{ srcApprox: boolean; srcLine: number; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":310},"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:310","src":"src/render.ts:394"},"level":0},{"id":"distJsPathFor","longname":"distJsPathFor","name":"distJsPathFor","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"dist `.js` path for a source file: sibling rootDistDir, same relative path.","params":[{"description":"The source file whose dist counterpart is wanted.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute path of the expected dist `.js` file.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":330},"order":10,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:330","src":"src/render.ts:435"},"level":0},{"id":"distMapperFor","longname":"distMapperFor","name":"distMapperFor","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reader mapper for the user's committed dist map, or `null` when missing or\nreferring to a different source (stale build, foreign map).","params":[{"description":"Absolute path of the committed dist `.js` file.","name":"distJs","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Absolute path of the original source file the map must reference.","name":"srcAbsPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Per-file notes accumulator.","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The lookup result — a mapper, or `null` when the map is missing/stale.","type":{"names":["Promise<DistMapperResult>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":343},"async":true,"order":11,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:343","src":"src/render.ts:449"},"level":0},{"id":"fail","longname":"fail","name":"fail","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the failure result shape.","params":[{"description":"The source file that failed.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}},{"description":"The planned output path.","name":"outPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Why the render failed.","name":"message","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Notes collected before the failure.","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The failure result.","type":{"names":["RenderFileResult"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":374},"order":12,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:374","src":"src/render.ts:484"},"level":0},{"id":"noteOnce","longname":"noteOnce","name":"noteOnce","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Adds an issue once per file.","params":[{"description":"The per-file notes accumulator (deduplicated in place).","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}},{"description":"The note to add.","name":"issue","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":382},"order":13,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:382","src":"src/render.ts:493"},"level":0},{"id":"withWarnSunk","longname":"withWarnSunk","name":"withWarnSunk","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Runs `fn` with `console.warn` silenced; the patch is never re-entered concurrently.","params":[{"description":"The operation whose warnings are sunk.","name":"fn","type":{"names":["() => Promise<T>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The operation's result.","type":{"names":["Promise<T>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":396},"async":true,"order":14,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/render.js:396","src":"src/render.ts:508"},"level":0}],"fp":"c1a4d16fe1b8164abf8a21953f7b26573e4d38e2ed96a85b9b4ca3b0c12a6973","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319252,"symbols":0},"md:src/render.mocked.test.ts":{"fp":"0e326c9b62f870a52eb131e11e31d0696fe21b501bfc37da637a7138053381f8","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#doclet\">doclet(lineno, kind, name)</a> ⇒ <code>{ kind: string; longname: string; meta: { filename: string; lineno: number; path: string; }; name: string; params: { description: string; name: string; }[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds a minimal doclet for tests (defaults: function/thing).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#setup\">setup(dir, files)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Writes <code>files</code> (name → content) under <code>&lt;dir&gt;/src</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#sourceFile\">sourceFile(relPath, extension, dir)</a> ⇒ <code>SourceFile</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds a SourceFile record for tests.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"doclet\"></a>\n\n## doclet(lineno, kind, name) ⇒ <code>{ kind: string; longname: string; meta: { filename: string; lineno: number; path: string; }; name: string; params: { description: string; name: string; }[]; }</code>\nBuilds a minimal doclet for tests (defaults: function/thing).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ kind: string; longname: string; meta: { filename: string; lineno: number; path: string; }; name: string; params: { description: string; name: string; }[]; }</code> - The doclet object.  \n\n| Param | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| lineno | <code>number</code> |  | The jsdoc-reported line number of the doclet. |\n| kind | <code>string</code> | <code>&quot;function&quot;</code> | The doclet kind. |\n| name | <code>string</code> | <code>&quot;thing&quot;</code> | The doclet name. |\n\nsrc: src/render.mocked.test.ts:36  \n<a name=\"setup\"></a>\n\n## setup(dir, files) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nWrites `files` (name → content) under `<dir>/src`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Nothing.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| dir | <code>string</code> | The fixture root to create. |\n| files | <code>Record&lt;string, string&gt;</code> | The files to write. |\n\nsrc: src/render.mocked.test.ts:52  \n<a name=\"sourceFile\"></a>\n\n## sourceFile(relPath, extension, dir) ⇒ <code>SourceFile</code>\nBuilds a SourceFile record for tests.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>SourceFile</code> - The SourceFile record.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| relPath | <code>string</code> | The posix-relative path of the source. |\n| extension | <code>&quot;.js&quot; \\| &quot;.jsx&quot; \\| &quot;.mjs&quot; \\| &quot;.cjs&quot; \\| &quot;.ts&quot; \\| &quot;.tsx&quot; \\| &quot;.mts&quot; \\| &quot;.cts&quot;</code> | The source extension. |\n| dir | <code>string</code> | The absolute project directory. |\n\nsrc: src/render.mocked.test.ts:66  \n","symbols":3},"md:src/doclet.test.ts":{"fp":"d6f39fc1aca7bd502db511fd130e098e657d279bbc9146558e4b9407f9a6d76c","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0},"md:src/cache.test.ts":{"fp":"b785837c864ddf0a99c4a57b5a105fec0f387cf844959f5cdf772907cebb9888","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"tmpdirOf\"></a>\n\n## tmpdirOf(prefix) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nCreates a self-cleaning temp directory.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The absolute path of the created directory.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| prefix | <code>string</code> | The mkdtemp prefix to use. |\n\nsrc: src/cache.test.ts:21  \n","symbols":1},"md:src/render.ts":{"fp":"94bc865c9fee552ca503b95c9d5f8ee183f6e193eecc5f742be1203e6074237f","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#DOCS_OVERRIDE\">DOCS_OVERRIDE</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The two handlebars partials injected into dmd.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#DIST_EXTENSION\">DIST_EXTENSION</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Dist extensions that differ from <code>source.slice(1)</code> (everything else strips the dot).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#renderSourceFile\">renderSourceFile(job, deps)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;RenderFileResult&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Renders one source file into markdown (or reports why it could not).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeTemplatePartials\">writeTemplatePartials(scratchDir)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Writes the two injected partials into the run&#39;s scratch directory.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#computePointers\">computePointers(file, data, transpileMapper, issues, pointerBase, distFolderMissing)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Map&lt;number, SymbolPointer&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Computes the per-doclet src/dist pointer map, keyed by generated line</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fetchTemplateData\">fetchTemplateData(scratchFile, deps, file, timeoutMs)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DmdDoclet[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Fetches template data for one file, reusing the tier-2 cache when possible.\nA cache hit skips the jsdoc child process; everything else (normalize,\npointer injection, checker types, render) still runs fresh.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#pointerPath\">pointerPath(base, absPath)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Renders an absolute path relative to the workspace root, posix-style.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#prepareForJsdoc\">prepareForJsdoc(file, srcText, scratchDir)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;PreparedFile&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Transpiles (.ts family) or copies (.js family) the source for jsdoc.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#resolveDistPointer\">resolveDistPointer(srcLine, transpileMapper, dist, issues)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Computes the dist pointer for one doclet. A missing dist folder (project probe)\nor dist file (per-file probe) omits the dist line entirely; when the dist map\nexists but the lookup misses, one &quot;dist sourcemap missing or unmatched&quot; note is\nrecorded instead.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#resolveSrcLine\">resolveSrcLine(generatedLine, transpileMapper)</a> ⇒ <code>{ srcApprox: boolean; srcLine: number; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Maps a doclet&#39;s generated line back to the original source line.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#distJsPathFor\">distJsPathFor(file)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>dist <code>.js</code> path for a source file: sibling rootDistDir, same relative path.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#distMapperFor\">distMapperFor(distJs, srcAbsPath, issues)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DistMapperResult&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Reader mapper for the user&#39;s committed dist map, or <code>null</code> when missing or\nreferring to a different source (stale build, foreign map).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fail\">fail(file, outPath, message, issues)</a> ⇒ <code>RenderFileResult</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Builds the failure result shape.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#noteOnce\">noteOnce(issues, issue)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Adds an issue once per file.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#withWarnSunk\">withWarnSunk(fn)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Runs <code>fn</code> with <code>console.warn</code> silenced; the patch is never re-entered concurrently.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"DOCS_OVERRIDE\"></a>\n\n## DOCS\\_OVERRIDE\nThe two handlebars partials injected into dmd.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/render.ts:69  \ndist: dist/render.js:40\n<a name=\"DIST_EXTENSION\"></a>\n\n## DIST\\_EXTENSION\nDist extensions that differ from `source.slice(1)` (everything else strips the dot).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/render.ts:405  \ndist: dist/render.js:319\n<a name=\"renderSourceFile\"></a>\n\n## renderSourceFile(job, deps) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;RenderFileResult&gt;</code>\nRenders one source file into markdown (or reports why it could not).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;RenderFileResult&gt;</code> - The render outcome (markdown, skip or failure) — always resolves.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| job | <code>RenderFileJob</code> | The file to render and its pool index. |\n| deps | <code>{ cache?: Cache; fingerprints?: ReadonlyMap&lt;string, FileFingerprints&gt;; missingDistDirs?: ReadonlySet&lt;string&gt;; outPath: string; partials: readonly string[]; pointerBase: string; scratchDir: string; timeoutMs?: number; typeProgram: null \\| TypeProgram; }</code> | Render-time dependencies (scratch dir, partials, output path, TS program, pointer base, jsdoc timeout). |\n| deps.cache |  | A loaded cache (absent ⇒ cache disabled). |\n| deps.fingerprints |  | The per-file cache fingerprints (absent ⇒ cache disabled). |\n| deps.missingDistDirs |  | Absolute distDirs known to be missing/not-directories (probed once per project by the run); for those projects no `dist:` line is emitted. |\n| deps.scratchDir |  | Per-file scratch directory for the transpiled/copied source. |\n| deps.partials |  | The handlebars partial override files (dmd template). |\n| deps.outPath |  | Where the generated markdown goes. |\n| deps.typeProgram |  | The project's TS program for checker types (null for JS files). |\n| deps.pointerBase |  | Absolute base for cwd-relative `src:`/`dist:` pointers. |\n| deps.timeoutMs |  | jsdoc render timeout in milliseconds. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:101  \ndist: dist/render.js:66\n<a name=\"writeTemplatePartials\"></a>\n\n## writeTemplatePartials(scratchDir) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code>\nWrites the two injected partials into the run's scratch directory.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code> - The absolute paths of the written partial files.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| scratchDir | <code>string</code> | Scratch directory that will hold `partials/`. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:194  \ndist: dist/render.js:128\n<a name=\"computePointers\"></a>\n\n## computePointers(file, data, transpileMapper, issues, pointerBase, distFolderMissing) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Map&lt;number, SymbolPointer&gt;&gt;</code>\nComputes the per-doclet src/dist pointer map, keyed by generated line\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Map&lt;number, SymbolPointer&gt;&gt;</code> - A generated-line → pointer map.  \n\n| Param | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> |  | The source file being rendered. |\n| data | <code>readonly DmdDoclet[]</code> |  | The doclets to annotate (already normalized). |\n| transpileMapper | <code>SourceLineMapper</code> |  | Mapper from the in-memory transpile, or `null` for pass-through copies. |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> |  | Per-file notes accumulator. |\n| pointerBase | <code>string</code> |  | Absolute base for cwd-relative `src:`/`dist:` pointers. |\n| distFolderMissing | <code>boolean</code> | <code>false</code> | `true` when the project's dist folder was probed missing; the dist lookup is skipped entirely. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:216  \ndist: dist/render.js:149\n<a name=\"fetchTemplateData\"></a>\n\n## fetchTemplateData(scratchFile, deps, file, timeoutMs) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DmdDoclet[]&gt;</code>\nFetches template data for one file, reusing the tier-2 cache when possible.\nA cache hit skips the jsdoc child process; everything else (normalize,\npointer injection, checker types, render) still runs fresh.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;DmdDoclet[]&gt;</code> - The normalized doclets.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| scratchFile | <code>string</code> | The transpiled/copied source inside the scratch dir. |\n| deps | <code>{ cache?: Cache; fingerprints?: ReadonlyMap&lt;string, FileFingerprints&gt;; }</code> | The render deps (may carry a `cache` and per-file `fingerprints`). |\n| deps.cache |  | The loaded cache, or absent when caching is disabled. |\n| deps.fingerprints |  | The per-file fingerprints, or absent when caching is disabled. |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file being rendered. |\n| timeoutMs | <code>number</code> | The jsdoc render timeout in milliseconds. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:255  \ndist: dist/render.js:180\n<a name=\"pointerPath\"></a>\n\n## pointerPath(base, absPath) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nRenders an absolute path relative to the workspace root, posix-style.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The posix-style relative path.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| base | <code>string</code> | The absolute base the returned path is relative to. |\n| absPath | <code>string</code> | The absolute path to render. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:295  \ndist: dist/render.js:213\n<a name=\"prepareForJsdoc\"></a>\n\n## prepareForJsdoc(file, srcText, scratchDir) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;PreparedFile&gt;</code>\nTranspiles (.ts family) or copies (.js family) the source for jsdoc.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;PreparedFile&gt;</code> - The prepared scratch file (or the transpile error).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file being prepared. |\n| srcText | <code>string</code> | The source text. |\n| scratchDir | <code>string</code> | Per-file scratch directory to write into. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:306  \ndist: dist/render.js:223\n<a name=\"resolveDistPointer\"></a>\n\n## resolveDistPointer(srcLine, transpileMapper, dist, issues) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nComputes the dist pointer for one doclet. A missing dist folder (project probe)\nor dist file (per-file probe) omits the dist line entirely; when the dist map\nexists but the lookup misses, one \"dist sourcemap missing or unmatched\" note is\nrecorded instead.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The `dist:` pointer line, or `undefined` when the dist line must be omitted.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| srcLine | <code>number</code> | The source (original) line for the symbol. |\n| transpileMapper | <code>SourceLineMapper</code> | Mapper from the transpile emit, or `null` for pass-through copies. |\n| dist | <code>DistPointerContext</code> | Dist lookup context (kind, mapper, pointer path) computed once per file. |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> | Per-file notes accumulator. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:373  \ndist: dist/render.js:291\n<a name=\"resolveSrcLine\"></a>\n\n## resolveSrcLine(generatedLine, transpileMapper) ⇒ <code>{ srcApprox: boolean; srcLine: number; }</code>\nMaps a doclet's generated line back to the original source line.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ srcApprox: boolean; srcLine: number; }</code> - The source line and whether it is approximate.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| generatedLine | <code>number</code> | The jsdoc-reported line in the generated file. |\n| transpileMapper | <code>SourceLineMapper</code> | Mapper from the transpile emit, or `null` for pass-through copies. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:394  \ndist: dist/render.js:310\n<a name=\"distJsPathFor\"></a>\n\n## distJsPathFor(file) ⇒ <code>string</code>\ndist `.js` path for a source file: sibling rootDistDir, same relative path.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The absolute path of the expected dist `.js` file.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file whose dist counterpart is wanted. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:435  \ndist: dist/render.js:330\n<a name=\"distMapperFor\"></a>\n\n## distMapperFor(distJs, srcAbsPath, issues) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;DistMapperResult&gt;</code>\nReader mapper for the user's committed dist map, or `null` when missing or\nreferring to a different source (stale build, foreign map).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;DistMapperResult&gt;</code> - The lookup result — a mapper, or `null` when the map is missing/stale.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| distJs | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the committed dist `.js` file. |\n| srcAbsPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the original source file the map must reference. |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> | Per-file notes accumulator. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:449  \ndist: dist/render.js:343\n<a name=\"fail\"></a>\n\n## fail(file, outPath, message, issues) ⇒ <code>RenderFileResult</code>\nBuilds the failure result shape.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>RenderFileResult</code> - The failure result.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file that failed. |\n| outPath | <code>string</code> | The planned output path. |\n| message | <code>string</code> | Why the render failed. |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> | Notes collected before the failure. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:484  \ndist: dist/render.js:374\n<a name=\"noteOnce\"></a>\n\n## noteOnce(issues, issue)\nAdds an issue once per file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> | The per-file notes accumulator (deduplicated in place). |\n| issue | <code>string</code> | The note to add. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:493  \ndist: dist/render.js:382\n<a name=\"withWarnSunk\"></a>\n\n## withWarnSunk(fn) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code>\nRuns `fn` with `console.warn` silenced; the patch is never re-entered concurrently.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code> - The operation's result.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| fn | <code>() &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;T&gt;</code> | The operation whose warnings are sunk. |\n\nsrc: src/render.ts:508  \ndist: dist/render.js:396\n","symbols":15},"tdata:src/resolve.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"DECLARATION_FILE","longname":"DECLARATION_FILE","name":"DECLARATION_FILE","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Declaration files (`.d.ts`/`.d.mts`/`.d.cts`) are not documentable — they carry no JSDoc.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":24},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:24","src":"src/resolve.ts:28"},"level":0},{"id":"collectSourceFiles","longname":"collectSourceFiles","name":"collectSourceFiles","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Recursively collects the documentable source files of every project,\nskipping `node_modules`, VCS internals, declaration files and the generated\ndocs directory itself. Returns the files plus any non-fatal notes (e.g.\nunreadable directories, which are skipped rather than aborting the run).\n\nThrows `MdocsError` `OUTPUT_COLLISION` when two source files would\nproduce the same `.md` path (e.g. `dup.ts` and `dup.mjs`) — that is a hard\nerror, not something to silently overwrite.","params":[{"description":"The resolved projects to collect from.","name":"projects","type":{"names":["readonly ProjectRoot[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The files plus any non-fatal notes (unreadable directories skipped).","type":{"names":["Promise<CollectResult>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":40},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:40","src":"src/resolve.ts:74"},"level":0},{"id":"isTypeScriptExtension","longname":"isTypeScriptExtension","name":"isTypeScriptExtension","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Narrows a raw extension to `.ts`-family (transpiled before jsdoc).","params":[{"description":"The source extension (with leading dot).","name":"extension","type":{"names":["\".js\" | \".jsx\" | \".mjs\" | \".cjs\" | \".ts\" | \".tsx\" | \".mts\" | \".cts\""]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` for `.ts`/`.tsx`/`.mts`/`.cts`.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":63},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:63","src":"src/resolve.ts:96"},"level":0},{"id":"outputPathFor","longname":"outputPathFor","name":"outputPathFor","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Output path for a source file: `<outDir>/<relPath with .md extension>`.\nContained by construction — `relPath` comes from `walkFiles(project.srcDir)`,\nso it is relative with no `..` ascent.","params":[{"description":"The source file being written out.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute output path for the `.md` file.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":73},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:73","src":"src/resolve.ts:107"},"level":0},{"id":"probeMissingDistDirs","longname":"probeMissingDistDirs","name":"probeMissingDistDirs","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Probes each project's dist folder exactly once. Missing or non-directory\ndist folders are returned so the run can omit dist pointers and warn.","params":[{"description":"The resolved projects to probe.","name":"projects","type":{"names":["readonly ProjectRoot[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute distDirs that are absent or not directories.","type":{"names":["Promise<Set<string>>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":83},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:83","src":"src/resolve.ts:118"},"level":0},{"id":"resolveProjects","longname":"resolveProjects","name":"resolveProjects","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Expands `config.rootSrcDir` to concrete `ProjectRoot`s.","params":[{"description":"The resolved config (roots and output directory names).","name":"config","type":{"names":["ResolvedMdocsConfig"]}},{"description":"Base directory for relative entries and glob expansion.","name":"cwd","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The resolved projects (one per src directory).","type":{"names":["Promise<ProjectRoot[]>"]}}],"exceptions":[{"type":{"names":["MdocsError"]},"description":"`NO_ROOTS` when nothing matches, `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS`\n  when one src dir contains another, `INVALID_ROOT` for unreadable/non-dir\n  entries."}],"meta":{"lineno":110},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:110","src":"src/resolve.ts:145"},"level":0},{"id":"toPosix","longname":"toPosix","name":"toPosix","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"POSIX-style relative path (forward slashes).","params":[{"description":"The path to normalize.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The path with forward slashes.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":146},"order":6,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:146","src":"src/resolve.ts:183"},"level":0},{"id":"walkFiles","longname":"walkFiles","name":"walkFiles","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Recursively lists files under `dir`, never following directory symlinks.","params":[{"description":"The directory to walk.","name":"dir","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Per-run notes accumulator (unreadable directories).","name":"issues","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The absolute paths of the files found.","type":{"names":["Promise<string[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":155},"order":7,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:155","src":"src/resolve.ts:193"},"level":0},{"id":"assertNoOutputCollisions","longname":"assertNoOutputCollisions","name":"assertNoOutputCollisions","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Fails the whole run when two files in one project would write the same\n`.md` — that is a configuration problem, not a rendering failure.","params":[{"description":"The collected files to check for colliding outputs.","name":"files","type":{"names":["readonly SourceFile[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":188},"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:188","src":"src/resolve.ts:223"},"level":0},{"id":"assertNoOverlappingRoots","longname":"assertNoOverlappingRoots","name":"assertNoOverlappingRoots","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Rejects roots where one src directory is nested inside another.","params":[{"description":"The resolved source directories to validate.","name":"roots","type":{"names":["readonly string[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":209},"order":9,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:209","src":"src/resolve.ts:243"},"level":0},{"id":"expandGlob","longname":"expandGlob","name":"expandGlob","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Expands a glob pattern against `cwd`, returning canonical directory paths.\nA pattern that matches only files is reported distinctly from one that\nmatches nothing at all.","params":[{"description":"The glob pattern to expand (against `cwd`).","name":"pattern","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Base directory for relative patterns.","name":"cwd","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The matched directories (absolute paths).","type":{"names":["Promise<string[]>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":231},"async":true,"order":10,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:231","src":"src/resolve.ts:269"},"level":0},{"id":"isSourceExtension","longname":"isSourceExtension","name":"isSourceExtension","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Narrows a raw extension to `SourceExtension`.","params":[{"description":"The raw extension to test.","name":"extension","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` for the eight supported source extensions.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":263},"order":11,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:263","src":"src/resolve.ts:301"},"level":0},{"id":"lowerExtension","longname":"lowerExtension","name":"lowerExtension","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Lower-cased file extension including the dot.","params":[{"description":"Absolute path of the file.","name":"absPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The lower-cased extension (with leading dot), or `''` for dotfiles.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":271},"order":12,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:271","src":"src/resolve.ts:310"},"level":0},{"id":"requireDirectory","longname":"requireDirectory","name":"requireDirectory","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Stats `path`, requiring an existing directory; returns its realpath.","params":[{"description":"The path to check.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The canonical (realpath) directory path.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":281},"async":true,"order":13,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/resolve.js:281","src":"src/resolve.ts:321"},"level":0}],"fp":"a62e849f1486cefa7e0fb979b87f8f58fa778dd456da8c56981213a67282cf18","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319568,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/schema.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"doclets","longname":"doclets","name":"doclets","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Raw `jsdoc2md.getTemplateData()` output (tdata entries only).","meta":{"lineno":143},"order":13,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:143","src":"src/schema.ts:179"},"level":0},{"id":"fp","longname":"fp","name":"fp","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Content fingerprint the entry was computed from.","meta":{"lineno":145},"order":14,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:145","src":"src/schema.ts:181"},"level":0},{"id":"issues","longname":"issues","name":"issues","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Notes the fresh render produced (replayed on tier-1 hits). Always stored — possibly empty.","meta":{"lineno":147},"order":15,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:147","src":"src/schema.ts:183"},"level":0},{"id":"lastUsed","longname":"lastUsed","name":"lastUsed","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Milliseconds since epoch of the last hit/store — drives LRU eviction.","meta":{"lineno":150},"order":16,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:150","src":"src/schema.ts:186"},"level":0},{"id":"markdown","longname":"markdown","name":"markdown","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"The finished markdown (md entries, non-skipped).","meta":{"lineno":152},"order":17,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:152","src":"src/schema.ts:188"},"level":0},{"id":"skipped","longname":"skipped","name":"skipped","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"The source file was intentionally not rendered (no JSDoc).","meta":{"lineno":154},"order":18,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:154","src":"src/schema.ts:190"},"level":0},{"id":"version","longname":"version","name":"version","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Cache format version — bump on incompatible changes.","meta":{"lineno":175},"order":20,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:175","src":"src/schema.ts:212"},"level":0},{"id":"ABSOLUTE_PATH","longname":"ABSOLUTE_PATH","name":"ABSOLUTE_PATH","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Matches POSIX absolute paths, Windows drive paths and UNC paths.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":21},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:21","src":"src/schema.ts:24"},"level":0},{"id":"DEFAULT_CONFIG","longname":"DEFAULT_CONFIG","name":"DEFAULT_CONFIG","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Default values for every configuration key. Single source for the schema\n`.default()` arguments and the public `DEFAULT_CONFIG` export.","meta":{"lineno":38},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:38","src":"src/schema.ts:43"},"level":0},{"id":"relativeDirName","longname":"relativeDirName","name":"relativeDirName","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Relative directory name allowed for `rootDistDir` / `outDirName` / `cachePath`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":47},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:47","src":"src/schema.ts:53"},"level":0},{"id":"rootSrcDirEntry","longname":"rootSrcDirEntry","name":"rootSrcDirEntry","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"One src dir: a path or glob pattern (unexpanded here — resolved later).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":56},"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:56","src":"src/schema.ts:66"},"level":0},{"id":"mdocsConfigSchema","longname":"mdocsConfigSchema","name":"mdocsConfigSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Validates `mdocs.config.*` content. Unknown keys are rejected (an\nunrecognized key is nearly always a typo'd option).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":61},"order":5,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:61","src":"src/schema.ts:72"},"level":0},{"id":"cacheEntryKind","longname":"cacheEntryKind","name":"cacheEntryKind","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Kind discriminator of one cache entry.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":136},"order":10,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:136","src":"src/schema.ts:170"},"level":0},{"id":"cacheKeySchema","longname":"cacheKeySchema","name":"cacheKeySchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Cache keys are `<kind>:<cwd-relative posix path>`, e.g. `md:src/cli.ts`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":138},"order":11,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:138","src":"src/schema.ts:173"},"level":0},{"id":"cacheEntrySchema","longname":"cacheEntrySchema","name":"cacheEntrySchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"One cache entry — either a finished render or raw jsdoc template data.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":140},"order":12,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:140","src":"src/schema.ts:176"},"level":0},{"id":"cacheFileSchema","longname":"cacheFileSchema","name":"cacheFileSchema","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"One on-disk render cache (see `cache.js`).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":172},"order":19,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:172","src":"src/schema.ts:209"},"level":0},{"id":"dirSegments","longname":"dirSegments","name":"dirSegments","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Splits a candidate relative dir name into its meaningful segments.","params":[{"description":"The candidate relative directory name.","name":"value","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The non-trivial path segments (never `.`, never empty).","type":{"names":["string[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":31},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:31","src":"src/schema.ts:35"},"level":0},{"id":"parseMdocsConfig","longname":"parseMdocsConfig","name":"parseMdocsConfig","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Parses `input` (config file content) into a validated object, throwing\n`MdocsError` with a message that names every offending key.","params":[{"description":"The unvalidated config input.","name":"input","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The validated config (all keys present; defaults applied).","type":{"names":["{ cache: boolean; cachePath: string; outDirName: string; parallelism: number | boolean; rootDistDir: string; rootSrcDir: string | string[]; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":80},"order":6,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:80","src":"src/schema.ts:98"},"level":0},{"id":"envFlag","longname":"envFlag","name":"envFlag","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Truthy interpretation for flag-style environment variables.","params":[{"description":"The raw env var value.","name":"value","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` for `1|true|yes|on` (case-insensitive), else `false`.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":91},"order":7,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:91","src":"src/schema.ts:109"},"level":0},{"id":"formatIssues","longname":"formatIssues","name":"formatIssues","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Flattens a ZodError into one `key: message` sentence per issue.","params":[{"description":"The ZodError whose issues are formatted.","name":"error","type":{"names":["z.ZodError<unknown>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A single-line, human-readable issue summary.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":102},"order":8,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:102","src":"src/schema.ts:122"},"level":0},{"id":"parseProcessEnv","longname":"parseProcessEnv","name":"parseProcessEnv","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Validates the environment variables mdocs consumes. Never throws: unknown\nvariables are ignored and invalid values fall back to safe defaults.","params":[{"description":"The raw environment (missing keys fall back to defaults).","name":"env","type":{"names":["NodeJS.ProcessEnv"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The parsed `NODE_ENV` value.","type":{"names":["ProcessEnv"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":122},"order":9,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:122","src":"src/schema.ts:154"},"level":0},{"id":"parseCacheFile","longname":"parseCacheFile","name":"parseCacheFile","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Parses the on-disk cache. Never throws: a corrupt or outdated cache is a\ncache miss, not a failure — the run simply re-renders.","params":[{"description":"The parsed JSON (unknown).","name":"input","type":{"names":["unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The validated cache, or `null` when missing/corrupt/unsupported.","type":{"names":["{ entries: Record<string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: \"md\" | \"tdata\"; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record<string, unknown>[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: \"no-jsdoc\"; }>; version: 1; }"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":183},"order":21,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/schema.js:183","src":"src/schema.ts:222"},"level":0}],"fp":"7531b3fba3a1dd7156f645071b19049a63361bbe02ae1c87eae2e24cb206ff5b","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319570,"symbols":0},"tdata:src/scratch.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"withScratch","longname":"withScratch","name":"withScratch","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Runs `fn` with a temporary scratch directory, removing it afterwards no\nmatter how `fn` exits.","params":[{"description":"The work to run with the scratch directory.","name":"fn","type":{"names":["(scratch: Scratch) => Promise<T>"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The value returned by `fn`.","type":{"names":["Promise<T>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":20},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/scratch.js:20","src":"src/scratch.ts:27"},"level":0}],"fp":"f22f8770f80852ad13bc6cc6eef2d4de7f3ee18df3320389b16e69aefa3ac8be","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319571,"symbols":0},"md:src/resolve.ts":{"fp":"b6a45bd67efc373ee51f20beb99e52f90fa5e3299a4ca3d73663637c499608e3","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#DECLARATION_FILE\">DECLARATION_FILE</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Declaration files (<code>.d.ts</code>/<code>.d.mts</code>/<code>.d.cts</code>) are not documentable — they carry no JSDoc.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#collectSourceFiles\">collectSourceFiles(projects)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;CollectResult&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Recursively collects the documentable source files of every project,\nskipping <code>node_modules</code>, VCS internals, declaration files and the generated\ndocs directory itself. Returns the files plus any non-fatal notes (e.g.\nunreadable directories, which are skipped rather than aborting the run).</p>\n<p>Throws <code>MdocsError</code> <code>OUTPUT_COLLISION</code> when two source files would\nproduce the same <code>.md</code> path (e.g. <code>dup.ts</code> and <code>dup.mjs</code>) — that is a hard\nerror, not something to silently overwrite.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isTypeScriptExtension\">isTypeScriptExtension(extension)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Narrows a raw extension to <code>.ts</code>-family (transpiled before jsdoc).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#outputPathFor\">outputPathFor(file)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Output path for a source file: <code>&lt;outDir&gt;/&lt;relPath with .md extension&gt;</code>.\nContained by construction — <code>relPath</code> comes from <code>walkFiles(project.srcDir)</code>,\nso it is relative with no <code>..</code> ascent.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#probeMissingDistDirs\">probeMissingDistDirs(projects)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Set&lt;string&gt;&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Probes each project&#39;s dist folder exactly once. Missing or non-directory\ndist folders are returned so the run can omit dist pointers and warn.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#resolveProjects\">resolveProjects(config, cwd)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;ProjectRoot[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Expands <code>config.rootSrcDir</code> to concrete <code>ProjectRoot</code>s.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#toPosix\">toPosix(path)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>POSIX-style relative path (forward slashes).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#walkFiles\">walkFiles(dir, issues)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Recursively lists files under <code>dir</code>, never following directory symlinks.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#assertNoOutputCollisions\">assertNoOutputCollisions(files)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Fails the whole run when two files in one project would write the same\n<code>.md</code> — that is a configuration problem, not a rendering failure.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#assertNoOverlappingRoots\">assertNoOverlappingRoots(roots)</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rejects roots where one src directory is nested inside another.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#expandGlob\">expandGlob(pattern, cwd)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Expands a glob pattern against <code>cwd</code>, returning canonical directory paths.\nA pattern that matches only files is reported distinctly from one that\nmatches nothing at all.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#isSourceExtension\">isSourceExtension(extension)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Narrows a raw extension to <code>SourceExtension</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#lowerExtension\">lowerExtension(absPath)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Lower-cased file extension including the dot.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#requireDirectory\">requireDirectory(path)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Stats <code>path</code>, requiring an existing directory; returns its realpath.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"DECLARATION_FILE\"></a>\n\n## DECLARATION\\_FILE\nDeclaration files (`.d.ts`/`.d.mts`/`.d.cts`) are not documentable — they carry no JSDoc.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/resolve.ts:28  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:24\n<a name=\"collectSourceFiles\"></a>\n\n## collectSourceFiles(projects) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;CollectResult&gt;</code>\nRecursively collects the documentable source files of every project,\nskipping `node_modules`, VCS internals, declaration files and the generated\ndocs directory itself. Returns the files plus any non-fatal notes (e.g.\nunreadable directories, which are skipped rather than aborting the run).\n\nThrows `MdocsError` `OUTPUT_COLLISION` when two source files would\nproduce the same `.md` path (e.g. `dup.ts` and `dup.mjs`) — that is a hard\nerror, not something to silently overwrite.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;CollectResult&gt;</code> - The files plus any non-fatal notes (unreadable directories skipped).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| projects | <code>readonly ProjectRoot[]</code> | The resolved projects to collect from. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:74  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:40\n<a name=\"isTypeScriptExtension\"></a>\n\n## isTypeScriptExtension(extension) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nNarrows a raw extension to `.ts`-family (transpiled before jsdoc).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` for `.ts`/`.tsx`/`.mts`/`.cts`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| extension | <code>&quot;.js&quot; \\| &quot;.jsx&quot; \\| &quot;.mjs&quot; \\| &quot;.cjs&quot; \\| &quot;.ts&quot; \\| &quot;.tsx&quot; \\| &quot;.mts&quot; \\| &quot;.cts&quot;</code> | The source extension (with leading dot). |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:96  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:63\n<a name=\"outputPathFor\"></a>\n\n## outputPathFor(file) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nOutput path for a source file: `<outDir>/<relPath with .md extension>`.\nContained by construction — `relPath` comes from `walkFiles(project.srcDir)`,\nso it is relative with no `..` ascent.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The absolute output path for the `.md` file.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file being written out. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:107  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:73\n<a name=\"probeMissingDistDirs\"></a>\n\n## probeMissingDistDirs(projects) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;Set&lt;string&gt;&gt;</code>\nProbes each project's dist folder exactly once. Missing or non-directory\ndist folders are returned so the run can omit dist pointers and warn.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;Set&lt;string&gt;&gt;</code> - The absolute distDirs that are absent or not directories.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| projects | <code>readonly ProjectRoot[]</code> | The resolved projects to probe. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:118  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:83\n<a name=\"resolveProjects\"></a>\n\n## resolveProjects(config, cwd) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;ProjectRoot[]&gt;</code>\nExpands `config.rootSrcDir` to concrete `ProjectRoot`s.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;ProjectRoot[]&gt;</code> - The resolved projects (one per src directory).  \n**Throws**:\n\n- <code>MdocsError</code> `NO_ROOTS` when nothing matches, `OVERLAPPING_ROOTS`\n  when one src dir contains another, `INVALID_ROOT` for unreadable/non-dir\n  entries.\n\n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| config | <code>ResolvedMdocsConfig</code> | The resolved config (roots and output directory names). |\n| cwd | <code>string</code> | Base directory for relative entries and glob expansion. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:145  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:110\n<a name=\"toPosix\"></a>\n\n## toPosix(path) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nPOSIX-style relative path (forward slashes).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The path with forward slashes.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The path to normalize. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:183  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:146\n<a name=\"walkFiles\"></a>\n\n## walkFiles(dir, issues) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code>\nRecursively lists files under `dir`, never following directory symlinks.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code> - The absolute paths of the files found.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| dir | <code>string</code> | The directory to walk. |\n| issues | <code>string[]</code> | Per-run notes accumulator (unreadable directories). |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:193  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:155\n<a name=\"assertNoOutputCollisions\"></a>\n\n## assertNoOutputCollisions(files)\nFails the whole run when two files in one project would write the same\n`.md` — that is a configuration problem, not a rendering failure.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| files | <code>readonly SourceFile[]</code> | The collected files to check for colliding outputs. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:223  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:188\n<a name=\"assertNoOverlappingRoots\"></a>\n\n## assertNoOverlappingRoots(roots)\nRejects roots where one src directory is nested inside another.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| roots | <code>readonly string[]</code> | The resolved source directories to validate. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:243  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:209\n<a name=\"expandGlob\"></a>\n\n## expandGlob(pattern, cwd) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code>\nExpands a glob pattern against `cwd`, returning canonical directory paths.\nA pattern that matches only files is reported distinctly from one that\nmatches nothing at all.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string[]&gt;</code> - The matched directories (absolute paths).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| pattern | <code>string</code> | The glob pattern to expand (against `cwd`). |\n| cwd | <code>string</code> | Base directory for relative patterns. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:269  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:231\n<a name=\"isSourceExtension\"></a>\n\n## isSourceExtension(extension) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nNarrows a raw extension to `SourceExtension`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` for the eight supported source extensions.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| extension | <code>string</code> | The raw extension to test. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:301  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:263\n<a name=\"lowerExtension\"></a>\n\n## lowerExtension(absPath) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nLower-cased file extension including the dot.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The lower-cased extension (with leading dot), or `''` for dotfiles.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| absPath | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the file. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:310  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:271\n<a name=\"requireDirectory\"></a>\n\n## requireDirectory(path) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\nStats `path`, requiring an existing directory; returns its realpath.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The canonical (realpath) directory path.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The path to check. |\n\nsrc: src/resolve.ts:321  \ndist: dist/resolve.js:281\n","symbols":14},"tdata:src/run.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"run","longname":"run","name":"run","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Executes the full pipeline. Resolves to a `RunResult`; throws only\nfor hard errors (config invalid, roots missing or overlapping).","params":[{"description":"Run options (cwd, config path, dry-run, inline config keys).","name":"options","type":{"names":["RunOptions"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The run result — written/skipped/failed files, notes, timings.","type":{"names":["Promise<RunResult>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":29},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/run.js:29","src":"src/run.ts:85"},"level":0},{"id":"cachedResult","longname":"cachedResult","name":"cachedResult","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Rebuilds a render result from a tier-1 cache entry.","params":[{"description":"The cached entry (fp already matched by the caller).","name":"entry","type":{"names":["{ fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: \"md\" | \"tdata\"; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record<string, unknown>[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: \"no-jsdoc\"; }"]}},{"description":"The source file the entry belongs to.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}},{"description":"The planned output path.","name":"outPath","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The render outcome (identical in shape to a fresh render).","type":{"names":["RenderFileResult"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":206},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/run.js:206","src":"src/run.ts:275"},"level":0},{"id":"storeCachedResult","longname":"storeCachedResult","name":"storeCachedResult","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Stores one successful render in the tier-1 cache (skips failures).","params":[{"description":"The loaded cache, or absent when caching is disabled.","name":"cache","type":{"names":["Cache"]}},{"description":"The file's fingerprints.","name":"fp","type":{"names":["FileFingerprints"]}},{"description":"The render outcome.","name":"result","type":{"names":["RenderFileResult"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":218},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/run.js:218","src":"src/run.ts:288"},"level":0},{"id":"tryOutputPath","longname":"tryOutputPath","name":"tryOutputPath","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Best-effort `outputPathFor` for the unreachable-error path.","params":[{"description":"The source file whose planned output path is wanted.","name":"file","type":{"names":["SourceFile"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The planned output path, or `<unresolved>` when it cannot be computed.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":237},"order":3,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/run.js:237","src":"src/run.ts:306"},"level":0},{"id":"writeMarkdown","longname":"writeMarkdown","name":"writeMarkdown","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Writes one rendered markdown file.","params":[{"description":"The file to write.","name":"target","type":{"names":["{ markdown: string; outPath: string; }"]}},{"description":"Absolute destination of the markdown.","name":"target.outPath"},{"description":"The markdown content.","name":"target.markdown"}],"returns":[{"description":"Nothing.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":253},"async":true,"order":4,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/run.js:253","src":"src/run.ts:322"},"level":0}],"fp":"ac52acd40826063da87dd0b10b28c9aa28770cdf9ca3df498014d477651c69e6","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319698,"symbols":0},"md:src/scratch.ts":{"fp":"5bc875ff2fd0fe5d3ba24891123bb5b7190c96984358d7e3582a4f942fae02b4","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"withScratch\"></a>\n\n## withScratch(fn) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code>\nRuns `fn` with a temporary scratch directory, removing it afterwards no\nmatter how `fn` exits.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;T&gt;</code> - The value returned by `fn`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| fn | <code>(scratch: Scratch) &#x3D;&gt; Promise&lt;T&gt;</code> | The work to run with the scratch directory. |\n\nsrc: src/scratch.ts:27  \ndist: dist/scratch.js:20\n","symbols":1},"tdata:src/test-utils.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"expectMdocsError","longname":"expectMdocsError","name":"expectMdocsError","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Asserts that `fn` throws an `MdocsError`, returning it for further\nassertions. Re-throws the original error untouched when it is not an\n`MdocsError`, so unexpected failure modes stay loud.","params":[{"description":"The function expected to throw an `MdocsError`.","name":"fn","type":{"names":["() => unknown"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The `MdocsError` it threw.","type":{"names":["Promise<MdocsError>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":15},"order":0,"mdocs":{"src":"src/test-utils.ts:17"},"level":0},{"id":"mkdirp","longname":"mkdirp","name":"mkdirp","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"`mkdir` with `recursive: true` always (tests only create fixture trees) —\ndelegated to jutilities' `ensureDirectory`.","params":[{"description":"The directory to create.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Nothing.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":32},"order":1,"mdocs":{"src":"src/test-utils.ts:33"},"level":0},{"id":"readUtf8","longname":"readUtf8","name":"readUtf8","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"`readFile` pinned to utf8.","params":[{"description":"The file to read.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The file contents as a utf8 string.","type":{"names":["Promise<string>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":40},"order":2,"mdocs":{"src":"src/test-utils.ts:42"},"level":0},{"id":"writeUtf8","longname":"writeUtf8","name":"writeUtf8","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"`writeFile` pinned to utf8 — tests only ever write source text.","params":[{"description":"The file to write.","name":"path","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The utf8 content to write.","name":"data","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"Nothing.","type":{"names":["Promise<void>"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":50},"order":3,"mdocs":{"src":"src/test-utils.ts:53"},"level":0}],"fp":"9130a4b7c82b62e4337e1a097e86464e37909ab785f099c02734ea6400877a5e","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319772,"symbols":0},"md:src/schema.ts":{"fp":"22b67dd608e57bba03ad4286d9b9fa2a596d153bb9e4bd5af72b64e00ad9d430","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#doclets\">doclets</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Raw <code>jsdoc2md.getTemplateData()</code> output (tdata entries only).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#fp\">fp</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Content fingerprint the entry was computed from.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#issues\">issues</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Notes the fresh render produced (replayed on tier-1 hits). Always stored — possibly empty.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#lastUsed\">lastUsed</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Milliseconds since epoch of the last hit/store — drives LRU eviction.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#markdown\">markdown</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The finished markdown (md entries, non-skipped).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#skipped\">skipped</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The source file was intentionally not rendered (no JSDoc).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#version\">version</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Cache format version — bump on incompatible changes.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#ABSOLUTE_PATH\">ABSOLUTE_PATH</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Matches POSIX absolute paths, Windows drive paths and UNC paths.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#DEFAULT_CONFIG\">DEFAULT_CONFIG</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Default values for every configuration key. Single source for the schema\n<code>.default()</code> arguments and the public <code>DEFAULT_CONFIG</code> export.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#relativeDirName\">relativeDirName</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Relative directory name allowed for <code>rootDistDir</code> / <code>outDirName</code> / <code>cachePath</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#rootSrcDirEntry\">rootSrcDirEntry</a></dt>\n<dd><p>One src dir: a path or glob pattern (unexpanded here — resolved later).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#mdocsConfigSchema\">mdocsConfigSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Validates <code>mdocs.config.*</code> content. Unknown keys are rejected (an\nunrecognized key is nearly always a typo&#39;d option).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cacheEntryKind\">cacheEntryKind</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Kind discriminator of one cache entry.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cacheKeySchema\">cacheKeySchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Cache keys are <code>&lt;kind&gt;:&lt;cwd-relative posix path&gt;</code>, e.g. <code>md:src/cli.ts</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cacheEntrySchema\">cacheEntrySchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>One cache entry — either a finished render or raw jsdoc template data.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#cacheFileSchema\">cacheFileSchema</a></dt>\n<dd><p>One on-disk render cache (see <code>cache.js</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#dirSegments\">dirSegments(value)</a> ⇒ <code>string[]</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Splits a candidate relative dir name into its meaningful segments.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseMdocsConfig\">parseMdocsConfig(input)</a> ⇒ <code>{ cache: boolean; cachePath: string; outDirName: string; parallelism: number | boolean; rootDistDir: string; rootSrcDir: string | string[]; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Parses <code>input</code> (config file content) into a validated object, throwing\n<code>MdocsError</code> with a message that names every offending key.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#envFlag\">envFlag(value)</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Truthy interpretation for flag-style environment variables.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#formatIssues\">formatIssues(error)</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Flattens a ZodError into one <code>key: message</code> sentence per issue.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseProcessEnv\">parseProcessEnv(env)</a> ⇒ <code>ProcessEnv</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Validates the environment variables mdocs consumes. Never throws: unknown\nvariables are ignored and invalid values fall back to safe defaults.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#parseCacheFile\">parseCacheFile(input)</a> ⇒ <code>{ entries: Record&lt;string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; | &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }&gt;; version: 1; }</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Parses the on-disk cache. Never throws: a corrupt or outdated cache is a\ncache miss, not a failure — the run simply re-renders.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"doclets\"></a>\n\n## doclets\nRaw `jsdoc2md.getTemplateData()` output (tdata entries only).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:179  \ndist: dist/schema.js:143\n<a name=\"fp\"></a>\n\n## fp\nContent fingerprint the entry was computed from.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:181  \ndist: dist/schema.js:145\n<a name=\"issues\"></a>\n\n## issues\nNotes the fresh render produced (replayed on tier-1 hits). Always stored — possibly empty.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:183  \ndist: dist/schema.js:147\n<a name=\"lastUsed\"></a>\n\n## lastUsed\nMilliseconds since epoch of the last hit/store — drives LRU eviction.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:186  \ndist: dist/schema.js:150\n<a name=\"markdown\"></a>\n\n## markdown\nThe finished markdown (md entries, non-skipped).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:188  \ndist: dist/schema.js:152\n<a name=\"skipped\"></a>\n\n## skipped\nThe source file was intentionally not rendered (no JSDoc).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:190  \ndist: dist/schema.js:154\n<a name=\"version\"></a>\n\n## version\nCache format version — bump on incompatible changes.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:212  \ndist: dist/schema.js:175\n<a name=\"ABSOLUTE_PATH\"></a>\n\n## ABSOLUTE\\_PATH\nMatches POSIX absolute paths, Windows drive paths and UNC paths.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:24  \ndist: dist/schema.js:21\n<a name=\"DEFAULT_CONFIG\"></a>\n\n## DEFAULT\\_CONFIG\nDefault values for every configuration key. Single source for the schema\n`.default()` arguments and the public `DEFAULT_CONFIG` export.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:43  \ndist: dist/schema.js:38\n<a name=\"relativeDirName\"></a>\n\n## relativeDirName\nRelative directory name allowed for `rootDistDir` / `outDirName` / `cachePath`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:53  \ndist: dist/schema.js:47\n<a name=\"rootSrcDirEntry\"></a>\n\n## rootSrcDirEntry\nOne src dir: a path or glob pattern (unexpanded here — resolved later).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:66  \ndist: dist/schema.js:56\n<a name=\"mdocsConfigSchema\"></a>\n\n## mdocsConfigSchema\nValidates `mdocs.config.*` content. Unknown keys are rejected (an\nunrecognized key is nearly always a typo'd option).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:72  \ndist: dist/schema.js:61\n<a name=\"cacheEntryKind\"></a>\n\n## cacheEntryKind\nKind discriminator of one cache entry.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:170  \ndist: dist/schema.js:136\n<a name=\"cacheKeySchema\"></a>\n\n## cacheKeySchema\nCache keys are `<kind>:<cwd-relative posix path>`, e.g. `md:src/cli.ts`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:173  \ndist: dist/schema.js:138\n<a name=\"cacheEntrySchema\"></a>\n\n## cacheEntrySchema\nOne cache entry — either a finished render or raw jsdoc template data.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:176  \ndist: dist/schema.js:140\n<a name=\"cacheFileSchema\"></a>\n\n## cacheFileSchema\nOne on-disk render cache (see `cache.js`).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/schema.ts:209  \ndist: dist/schema.js:172\n<a name=\"dirSegments\"></a>\n\n## dirSegments(value) ⇒ <code>string[]</code>\nSplits a candidate relative dir name into its meaningful segments.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string[]</code> - The non-trivial path segments (never `.`, never empty).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>string</code> | The candidate relative directory name. |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:35  \ndist: dist/schema.js:31\n<a name=\"parseMdocsConfig\"></a>\n\n## parseMdocsConfig(input) ⇒ <code>{ cache: boolean; cachePath: string; outDirName: string; parallelism: number \\| boolean; rootDistDir: string; rootSrcDir: string \\| string[]; }</code>\nParses `input` (config file content) into a validated object, throwing\n`MdocsError` with a message that names every offending key.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ cache: boolean; cachePath: string; outDirName: string; parallelism: number \\| boolean; rootDistDir: string; rootSrcDir: string \\| string[]; }</code> - The validated config (all keys present; defaults applied).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| input | <code>unknown</code> | The unvalidated config input. |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:98  \ndist: dist/schema.js:80\n<a name=\"envFlag\"></a>\n\n## envFlag(value) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nTruthy interpretation for flag-style environment variables.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` for `1|true|yes|on` (case-insensitive), else `false`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| value | <code>string</code> | The raw env var value. |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:109  \ndist: dist/schema.js:91\n<a name=\"formatIssues\"></a>\n\n## formatIssues(error) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nFlattens a ZodError into one `key: message` sentence per issue.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - A single-line, human-readable issue summary.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| error | <code>z.ZodError&lt;unknown&gt;</code> | The ZodError whose issues are formatted. |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:122  \ndist: dist/schema.js:102\n<a name=\"parseProcessEnv\"></a>\n\n## parseProcessEnv(env) ⇒ <code>ProcessEnv</code>\nValidates the environment variables mdocs consumes. Never throws: unknown\nvariables are ignored and invalid values fall back to safe defaults.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>ProcessEnv</code> - The parsed `NODE_ENV` value.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| env | <code>NodeJS.ProcessEnv</code> | The raw environment (missing keys fall back to defaults). |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:154  \ndist: dist/schema.js:122\n<a name=\"parseCacheFile\"></a>\n\n## parseCacheFile(input) ⇒ <code>{ entries: Record&lt;string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; \\| &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }&gt;; version: 1; }</code>\nParses the on-disk cache. Never throws: a corrupt or outdated cache is a\ncache miss, not a failure — the run simply re-renders.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>{ entries: Record&lt;string, { fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; \\| &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }&gt;; version: 1; }</code> - The validated cache, or `null` when missing/corrupt/unsupported.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| input | <code>unknown</code> | The parsed JSON (unknown). |\n\nsrc: src/schema.ts:222  \ndist: dist/schema.js:183\n","symbols":22},"tdata:src/tscheck.test.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"lookup","longname":"lookup","name":"lookup","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Looks up `name` (optionally qualified) in `file` of the shared program.","params":[{"description":"The shared type program under test.","name":"program","type":{"names":["import(\"./tscheck.js\").TypeProgram"]}},{"description":"Absolute path of the fixture source.","name":"file","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The plain symbol name to look up.","name":"name","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"The qualified lookup key (overrides the plain one).","name":"qualified","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The extracted types, or `null`.","type":{"names":["import(\"./tscheck.js\").SymbolType"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":20},"order":0,"mdocs":{"src":"src/tscheck.test.ts:23"},"level":0}],"fp":"cae2e0c35ee963652eccb0ce1734f879bc2c0f5451e1ec53b3fe1a20f07ecf48","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1794816319873,"symbols":0},"md:src/test-utils.ts":{"fp":"d4e8e0c6a0da70d621dbb29953c610aec95b630357e5e2c444475a82a71b31f0","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#expectMdocsError\">expectMdocsError(fn)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;MdocsError&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Asserts that <code>fn</code> throws an <code>MdocsError</code>, returning it for further\nassertions. Re-throws the original error untouched when it is not an\n<code>MdocsError</code>, so unexpected failure modes stay loud.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#mkdirp\">mkdirp(path)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p><code>mkdir</code> with <code>recursive: true</code> always (tests only create fixture trees) —\ndelegated to jutilities&#39; <code>ensureDirectory</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readUtf8\">readUtf8(path)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p><code>readFile</code> pinned to utf8.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#writeUtf8\">writeUtf8(path, data)</a> ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p><code>writeFile</code> pinned to utf8 — tests only ever write source text.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"expectMdocsError\"></a>\n\n## expectMdocsError(fn) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;MdocsError&gt;</code>\nAsserts that `fn` throws an `MdocsError`, returning it for further\nassertions. Re-throws the original error untouched when it is not an\n`MdocsError`, so unexpected failure modes stay loud.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;MdocsError&gt;</code> - The `MdocsError` it threw.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| fn | <code>() &#x3D;&gt; unknown</code> | The function expected to throw an `MdocsError`. |\n\nsrc: src/test-utils.ts:17  \n<a name=\"mkdirp\"></a>\n\n## mkdirp(path) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n`mkdir` with `recursive: true` always (tests only create fixture trees) —\ndelegated to jutilities' `ensureDirectory`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Nothing.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The directory to create. |\n\nsrc: src/test-utils.ts:33  \n<a name=\"readUtf8\"></a>\n\n## readUtf8(path) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code>\n`readFile` pinned to utf8.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;string&gt;</code> - The file contents as a utf8 string.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The file to read. |\n\nsrc: src/test-utils.ts:42  \n<a name=\"writeUtf8\"></a>\n\n## writeUtf8(path, data) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\n`writeFile` pinned to utf8 — tests only ever write source text.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Nothing.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| path | <code>string</code> | The file to write. |\n| data | <code>string</code> | The utf8 content to write. |\n\nsrc: src/test-utils.ts:53  \n","symbols":4},"tdata:src/version.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"packageVersion","longname":"packageVersion","name":"packageVersion","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Reads the mdocs package version from the packaged `package.json`.","returns":[{"description":"The version, or `0.0.0-unknown` when it is unreadable.","type":{"names":["string"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":12},"order":0,"mdocs"