from a tier-1 cache entry.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>RenderFileResult</code> - The render outcome (identical in shape to a fresh render).  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| entry | <code>{ fp: string; issues: string[]; kind: &quot;md&quot; \\| &quot;tdata&quot;; lastUsed: number; symbols: number; doclets?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;[]; markdown?: string; skipped?: &quot;no-jsdoc&quot;; }</code> | The cached entry (fp already matched by the caller). |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file the entry belongs to. |\n| outPath | <code>string</code> | The planned output path. |\n\nsrc: src/run.ts:275  \ndist: dist/run.js:206\n<a name=\"storeCachedResult\"></a>\n\n## storeCachedResult(cache, fp, result)\nStores one successful render in the tier-1 cache (skips failures).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cache | <code>Cache</code> | The loaded cache, or absent when caching is disabled. |\n| fp | <code>FileFingerprints</code> | The file's fingerprints. |\n| result | <code>RenderFileResult</code> | The render outcome. |\n\nsrc: src/run.ts:288  \ndist: dist/run.js:218\n<a name=\"tryOutputPath\"></a>\n\n## tryOutputPath(file) ⇒ <code>string</code>\nBest-effort `outputPathFor` for the unreachable-error path.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The planned output path, or `<unresolved>` when it cannot be computed.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| file | <code>SourceFile</code> | The source file whose planned output path is wanted. |\n\nsrc: src/run.ts:306  \ndist: dist/run.js:237\n<a name=\"writeMarkdown\"></a>\n\n## writeMarkdown(target) ⇒ <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code>\nWrites one rendered markdown file.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>Promise&lt;void&gt;</code> - Nothing.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| target | <code>{ markdown: string; outPath: string; }</code> | The file to write. |\n| target.outPath |  | Absolute destination of the markdown. |\n| target.markdown |  | The markdown content. |\n\nsrc: src/run.ts:322  \ndist: dist/run.js:253\n","symbols":5},"md:src/tscheck.test.ts":{"fp":"8539f2b2f127f1ab847b5c757913f69b77a6797506bb3083c8888a10dfcd7066","issues":["dist file not found — dist: line omitted (build first)"],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"lookup\"></a>\n\n## lookup(program, file, name, qualified) ⇒ <code>import(&quot;./tscheck.js&quot;).SymbolType</code>\nLooks up `name` (optionally qualified) in `file` of the shared program.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>import(&quot;./tscheck.js&quot;).SymbolType</code> - The extracted types, or `null`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| program | <code>import(&quot;./tscheck.js&quot;).TypeProgram</code> | The shared type program under test. |\n| file | <code>string</code> | Absolute path of the fixture source. |\n| name | <code>string</code> | The plain symbol name to look up. |\n| qualified | <code>string</code> | The qualified lookup key (overrides the plain one). |\n\nsrc: src/tscheck.test.ts:23  \n","symbols":1},"md:src/version.ts":{"fp":"a73c472a45ce55d1e83ed139aa4394d0bc7bf0b7b0628845ff9bbefb783f4726","issues":[],"kind":"md","lastUsed":1794817499055,"markdown":"<a name=\"packageVersion\"></a>\n\n## packageVersion() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nReads the mdocs package version from the packaged `package.json`.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \n**Returns**: <code>string</code> - The version, or `0.0.0-unknown` when it is unreadable.  \nsrc: src/version.ts:13  \ndist: dist/version.js:12\n","symbols":1},"tdata:src/tscheck.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"createTypeProgram","longname":"createTypeProgram","name":"createTypeProgram","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Builds the shared program for `files` (.ts family only). Compiler options\nare deliberately lenient: the program exists to read types, not to\ntype-check, so diagnostics are ignored.","params":[{"description":"The `.ts` family files to include in the program.","name":"files","type":{"names":["readonly string[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The shared program, or `null` for an empty file list.","type":{"names":["TypeProgram"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":28},"order":0,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/tscheck.js:28","src":"src/tscheck.ts:77"},"level":0},{"id":"lookupSymbol","longname":"lookupSymbol","name":"lookupSymbol","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Looks up extracted types for a doclet. Qualified lookup wins; a plain-name\nmatch is used only when it is unambiguous within the file. Returns `null`\nwhen nothing usable was found.","params":[{"description":"The shared type program.","name":"program","type":{"names":["TypeProgram"]}},{"description":"Absolute path of the source file to look up.","name":"srcAbsPath","type":{"names":["string"]}},{"description":"Qualified-first lookup keys for the doclet.","name":"lookup","type":{"names":["SymbolLookup"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The extracted types, or `null` when nothing usable was found.","type":{"names":["SymbolType"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":69},"order":1,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/tscheck.js:69","src":"src/tscheck.ts:117"},"level":0},{"id":"boundLeaves","longname":"boundLeaves","name":"boundLeaves","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Every identifier bound inside a (possibly nested) object/array pattern.","params":[{"description":"The binding pattern to walk.","name":"pattern","type":{"names":["ts.ArrayBindingPattern | ts.ObjectBindingPattern"]}},{"description":"Accumulator (recursion carries it) — name + declaring node.","name":"out","type":{"names":["{ name: string; node: ts.BindingElement; }[]"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"The bound leaves (name + node), in source order.","type":{"names":["{ name: string; node: ts.BindingElement; }[]"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":87},"order":2,"mdocs":{"dist":"dist/tscheck.js:87","src":"src/tscheck.ts:134"},